uality\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Sales","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"remote","location":"Remote","skills":["Prospecting","Cold Outreach","CRM","Communication"],"reqs":["6+ months to 2 years in B2B SDR, lead generation, or agency business development.","Sharp, natural written English—zero spammy template vibes.","High curiosity about websites, e-commerce, and digital products.","Organized self-starter comfortable with daily outreach targets in a remote team."],"lo":1100,"hi":1800,"days":16,"hours":7},{"company":"Nimbus Cloud","title":"Full-Stack Engineer (TypeScript)","description":"Nimbus Cloud builds cloud invoicing, automated payroll, and cash-flow software trusted by over 65,000 small businesses across North America. Headquartered in Toronto with remote product squads, we obsess over speed, auditability, and calm financial workflows. We're hiring a Full-Stack Engineer (TypeScript) to join the team (remote).\n\nAbout the role:\nOwn vertical product slices across Nimbus's core invoicing and recurring-billing platform—from PostgreSQL schema migrations and GraphQL/Node APIs to polished React UI.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Build end-to-end features across our React frontend, Node.js/TypeScript APIs, and PostgreSQL database.\n- Design safe, backward-compatible database migrations and efficient transactional queries.\n- Collaborate with product managers and designers early to scope edge cases around taxes, currencies, and PDF invoices.\n- Write unit, integration, and end-to-end tests that keep financial state rock-solid.\n- Monitor feature rollouts via feature flags, metrics, and error tracking.\n\nRequirements:\n- 3+ years of full-stack product engineering experience in TypeScript, React, and Node.js.\n- Strong relational database skills in PostgreSQL and API experience (GraphQL or REST).\n- Track record owning features independently from technical design through production monitoring.\n- High care for code clarity, automated testing, and user empathy.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience building fintech, accounting, billing, or B2B SaaS products.\n- Familiarity with AWS (Lambda, SQS, RDS) or Next.js.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Remote)\n- Extended health, dental, vision, and mental health benefits from day one\n- 22 days paid vacation plus company-wide December recharge week\n- RRSP/401k employer matching and $1,500/year learning budget\n- Home-office setup grant and quarterly virtual team budgets\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Software","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"remote","location":"Remote","skills":["TypeScript","React","Node.js","PostgreSQL","GraphQL","AWS","Testing"],"reqs":["3+ years of full-stack product engineering experience in TypeScript, React, and Node.js.","Strong relational database skills in PostgreSQL and API experience (GraphQL or REST).","Track record owning features independently from technical design through production monitoring.","High care for code clarity, automated testing, and user empathy."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":2,"hours":12},{"company":"Nimbus Cloud","title":"Senior Frontend Engineer","description":"Nimbus Cloud builds cloud invoicing, automated payroll, and cash-flow software trusted by over 65,000 small businesses across North America. Headquartered in Toronto with remote product squads, we obsess over speed, auditability, and calm financial workflows. We're hiring a Senior Frontend Engineer to join the team (remote).\n\nAbout the role:\nSet frontend technical direction across Nimbus Cloud's 30-engineer product org—leading our accessible design system, keyboard-first workflows, and client performance architecture.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Architect and maintain Nimbus's accessible React + TypeScript design system used by six product squads.\n- Lead complex, high-density UI workflows (multi-line invoice editors, bank-feed reconciliation grids) with 60fps responsiveness.\n- Drive frontend performance budgets, bundle splitting, and WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility compliance.\n- Write technical RFCs and partner with Staff Engineers on state management and caching patterns.\n- Mentor mid and junior frontend engineers through pairing, code reviews, and guild talks.\n\nRequirements:\n- 5+ years of frontend engineering experience building complex, data-rich React and TypeScript applications.\n- Deep mastery of browser rendering, React performance profiling, accessibility (ARIA/keyboard nav), and state architecture.\n- Proven experience building or scaling a multi-team component library / design system.\n- Strong technical leadership, mentoring, and written communication skills.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience with Next.js App Router, Radix UI primitives, and Playwright visual/a11y testing.\n- Background in accounting, spreadsheets, or B2B SaaS workflows.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $3,300–$5,000 USD / month (Full-time, Remote)\n- Extended health, dental, vision, and mental health benefits from day one\n- 22 days paid vacation plus company-wide December recharge week\n- RRSP/401k employer matching and $1,500/year learning budget\n- Home-office setup grant and quarterly virtual team budgets\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-f