hing, and statutory filing services powering Nimbus Payroll from our Toronto hub.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Develop deterministic payroll calculation, tax withholding, and year-end filing services in Python (Django/FastAPI).\n- Design resilient asynchronous background job pipelines with Celery/Redis and idempotent retries.\n- Optimize PostgreSQL data models for strict financial auditability and multi-year history.\n- Partner with compliance specialists to codify updated federal/provincial/state tax rules accurately.\n- Maintain high automated test coverage across edge-case pay runs and rounding rules.\n\nRequirements:\n- 3+ years of backend engineering experience in Python with Django or FastAPI.\n- Strong production proficiency with PostgreSQL, Redis, background workers, and Docker.\n- Disciplined habits around decimal precision, idempotency, and automated regression testing.\n- Ability to collaborate hybrid from our Toronto office 2 days/week.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience in payroll, HRIS, tax engines, or accounting software.\n- Familiarity with AWS ECS/RDS and Terraform.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- Extended health, dental, vision, and mental health benefits from day one\n- 22 days paid vacation plus company-wide December recharge week\n- RRSP/401k employer matching and $1,500/year learning budget\n- Home-office setup grant and quarterly virtual team budgets\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Software","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Toronto, Canada","skills":["Python","Django","PostgreSQL","Docker","REST APIs","Redis"],"reqs":["3+ years of backend engineering experience in Python with Djang