ement prompt-injection defenses, PII redaction, caching, and fallback routing across model tiers.\n- Monitor token usage, latency p95, and cost-per-task telemetry in production.\n- Work closely with product designers to surface AI confidence and human-in-the-loop review controls.\n\nRequirements:\n- 2+ years building backend/full-stack software in Python or TypeScript, plus 1+ year shipping LLM features to real users.\n- Hands-on experience with structured JSON outputs, embeddings/RAG (pgvector), and automated evals.\n- Strong engineering pragmatism around latency budgets, retries, caching, and prompt-injection safety.\n- Ability to clearly document model limitations and failure modes.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience with Gemini or OpenAI multimodal PDF/receipt parsing.\n- Familiarity with OCR or financial document classification.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Remote)\n- Extended health, dental, vision, and mental health benefits from day one\n- 22 days paid vacation plus company-wide December recharge week\n- RRSP/401k employer matching and $1,500/year learning budget\n- Home-office setup grant and quarterly virtual team budgets\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Software","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"remote","location":"Remote","skills":["Python","TypeScript","LLMs","RAG","PostgreSQL","Evals"],"reqs":["2+ years building backend/full-stack software in Python or TypeScript, plus 1+ year shipping LLM features to real users.","Hands-on experience with structured JSON outputs, embeddings/RAG (pgvector), and automated evals.","Strong engineering pragmatism around latency budgets, retries, caching, and prompt-injection safety.