ensive family medical insurance and life assurance\n- Complimentary employee mobile & home fiber plan plus device discounts\n- 21 days paid annual leave and annual performance bonus\n- Structured technical academy with Cisco, cloud, and telecom certifications\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Software","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Amman, Jordan","skills":["Kotlin","Android","Jetpack Compose","REST APIs","Git"],"reqs":["2+ years of native Android development experience using Kotlin.","Hands-on experience with Jetpack Compose, Coroutines/Flow, and MVVM/Clean Architecture.","Proven experience shipping and maintaining apps on Google Play.","Solid understanding of REST APIs, offline caching, and Android security best practices."],"lo":1300,"hi":2300,"days":2,"hours":9},{"company":"Skyline Telecom","title":"Telecommunications Engineer","description":"Skyline Telecom operates nationwide 4G/5G mobile networks, FTTH fiber broadband, and enterprise cloud connectivity for over 3.2 million subscribers in Jordan. Our engineering and digital teams modernize both physical radio/fiber infrastructure and self-service customer apps. We're hiring a Telecommunications Engineer to join the team (on-site, Amman, Jordan).\n\nAbout the role:\nPlan, tune, and optimize 4G LTE and 5G NR radio coverage alongside FTTH backhaul rollouts across urban and highway corridors in Jordan.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Perform RF link budgets, propagation modeling, and site candidate evaluations for new 4G/5G macro and small-cell sites.\n- Analyze RAN KPIs (drop rate, handover success, PRB utilization, SINR) to resolve congestion and interference.\n- Plan antenna azimuth/tilt optimizations and neighbor-list parameter tuning.\n- Coordinate with fiber-transmission and field-rigging teams during new site integration and drive tests.\n- Prepare coverage reports and capacity expansion forecasts for regional network planning.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's degree in Telecommunications or Electrical Engineering.\n- 2+ years in cellular RF planning, RAN optimization, or telecom field engineering (LTE/5G).\n- Proficiency with RF planning/post-processing tools (Atoll, TEMS, Actix, or OSS counters).\n- Willingness to conduct occasional regional field drive tests across Jordan.\n\nNice to have:\n- Hands-on experience with Ericsson, Huawei, or Nokia 5G RAN OSS platforms.\n- Valid Jordanian driving license.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,300–$2,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive family medical insurance and life assurance\n- Complimentary employee mobile & home fiber plan plus device discounts\n- 21 days paid annual leave and annual performance bonus\n- Structured technical academy with Cisco, cloud, and telecom certifications\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Engineering","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Amman, Jordan","skills":["RF Planning","LTE/5G","Network Optimization","Fiber Optics","Troubleshooting"],"reqs":["Bachelor's degree in Telecommunications or Electrical Engineering.","2+ years in cellular RF planning, RAN optimization, or telecom field engineering (LTE/5G).","Proficiency with RF planning/post-processing tools (Atoll, TEMS, Actix, or OSS counters).","Willingness to conduct occasional regional field drive tests across Jordan."],"lo":1300,"hi":2300,"days":9,"hours":14},{"company":"Skyline Telecom","title":"Network Engineer","description":"Skyline Telecom operates nationwide 4G/5G 