 monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Engineering","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Amman, Jordan","skills":["Networking","Cisco","Routing & Switching","Firewalls","Linux"],"reqs":["Bachelor's in Computer/Network Engineering or equivalent experience, with CCNP/CCNA-level mastery.","2+ years managing enterprise or ISP routing/switching (BGP, OSPF, VLANs, STP) and firewalls.","Strong hands-on experience with Cisco IOS/NX-OS, Juniper, or Fortinet/Palo Alto gear.","Comfort participating in an equitable on-call rotation for critical network escalations."],"lo":1300,"hi":2300,"days":16,"hours":19},{"company":"Skyline Telecom","title":"QA/QC Engineer","description":"Skyline Telecom operates nationwide 4G/5G mobile networks, FTTH fiber broadband, and enterprise cloud connectivity for over 3.2 million subscribers in Jordan. Our engineering and digital teams modernize both physical radio/fiber infrastructure and self-service customer apps. We're hiring a QA/QC Engineer to join the team (on-site, Amman, Jordan).\n\nAbout the role:\nEnsure telecom tower civil works, FTTH fiber trenching, and indoor distribution systems meet strict engineering, safety, and ISO 9001 quality standards.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Conduct on-site quality inspections for fiber splicing, OTDR testing, tower grounding, and power cabinets.\n- Verify contractor installations against approved drawings, Material Approval Requests (MAR), and ITPs.\n- Issue Non-Conformance Reports (NCRs) for defects and verify corrective actions before sign-off.\n- Maintain complete audit-ready QC dossiers and handover packages for telecom rollout phases.\n- Coordinate weekly quality reviews with rollout project managers and subcontractors.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's degree in Electrical, Telecom, or Civil Engineering.\n- 2+ years in QA/QC inspection on telecom, fiber, or infrastructure projects.\n- Strong working knowledge of ISO 9001 quality systems, ITPs, and OTDR/power-meter test validation.\n- Willingness to travel across site locations in Jordan with valid driver's license.\n\nNice to have:\n- ISO 9001 Lead Auditor or Fiber Optic Association (FOA) certification.\n- Experience supervising FTTH GPON rollouts.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,300–$2,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive family medical insurance and life assurance\n- Complimentary employee mobile & home fiber plan plus device discounts\n- 21 days paid annual leave and annual performance bonus\n- Structured technical academy with Cisco, cloud, and telecom certifications\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Engineering","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Amman, Jordan","skills":["Quality Control","Inspection","ISO 9001","Documentation","Site Supervision"],"reqs":["Bachelor's degree in Electrical, Telecom, or Civil Engineering.","2+ years in QA/QC inspection on telecom, fiber, or infrastructure projects.","Strong working knowledge of ISO 9001 quality systems, ITPs, and OTDR/power-meter test validation.","Willingness to travel across site locations in Jordan with valid driver's license."],"lo":1300,"hi":2300,"days":2,"hours":0},{"company":"Gulfstream Capital","title":"Data Engineer","description":"Gulfstream Capital is a DIFC-regulated asset management firm overseeing $3.8B across MENA public equities, sovereign/corporate fixed income, and quantitative multi-asset strategies for institutional and family-office clients. We're hiring a Data Engineer to join the team (hybrid, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nBuild reliable market-data, portfolio-accounting, and ESG data pipelines feeding Gulfstream's quantitative research and investor-reporting warehouse in Dubai.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Design and maintain daily and intraday ingestion pipelines in Python and Airflow from Bloomberg, Refinitiv, and custodian feeds.\n- Transform and test curated analytical models in dbt and Snowflake with strict data-quality assertions.\n- Optimize warehouse compute costs, partitioning, and SLA monitoring so morning risk reports arrive on time.\n- Partner with quantitative analysts and portfolio managers to onboard new alternative datasets.\n- Maintain audit lineage, access controls, and clear schema documentation.\n\nRequirements:\n- 3+ years of data engineering experience building production ETL/ELT pipelines in Python and SQL.\n- Hands-on expertise with dbt, Apache Airflow (or Dagster), Snowflake (or BigQuery), and AWS.\n- Strong software engineering habits: automated data tests, CI/CD, idempotent backfills.\n- High accuracy and discretion handling confidential institutional investment data.\n\nNice to have:\n- Domain experience in asset management, capital markets, or financial data feeds.\n- Familiarity with Parquet/Iceberg or time-series tick storage.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- DIFC-grade family medical coverage, life insurance, and annual flight ticket\n- 25 days paid annual leave plus performance-linked annual bonus\n- Full sponsorship for CFA, CAIA, or CQF study materials and exam fees\n- Modern DIFC office with Bloomberg terminals and research library\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call covering background, role scope, and monthly compensation alignment\n- 2. Practical role exercise (portfolio walkthrough or real-world technical pairing — no trick whiteboard puzzles)\n- 3. Final conversation with the hiring manager and cross-functional peers","field":"Software","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Python","SQL","Airflow","dbt","Snowflake","