, and chronic condition follow-ups.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Conduct thorough outpatient consultations, physical examinations, and evidence-based diagnostic workups.\n- Manage chronic conditions including hypertension, diabetes, asthma, and thyroid disorders.\n- Order and interpret routine laboratory and diagnostic imaging studies, coordinating referrals to hospital specialists.\n- Maintain clear, timely clinical documentation and e-prescriptions in our hospital EMR.\n- Deliver warm, culturally sensitive patient education on preventive health and lifestyle management.\n\nRequirements:\n- Medical degree (MD/MBBS) and active DHA license (or DHA eligibility letter) as a General Practitioner.\n- 2+ years of post-internship clinical experience in primary care or family medicine.\n- Strong clinical judgment, safe prescribing habits, and clear EMR documentation.\n- Fluent English; Arabic, Hindi, or Tagalog is a strong advantage for Dubai's diverse patients.\n\nNice to have:\n- MRCGP, Arab Board, or Family Medicine diploma.\n- Prior outpatient clinic experience within the UAE.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $3,200–$5,000 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- VIP family medical insurance, malpractice coverage, and DHA license fee reimbursement\n- 30 calendar days paid annual leave plus annual return flight allowance\n- Dedicated paid CME leave (7 days/year) and conference grant\n- Relocation package and housing support for international physicians\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Credential, degree, and active clinical license verification\n- 2. 45-minute clinical case discussion with the department lead\n- 3. Facility tour, schedule alignment, and Medical Director sign-off","field":"Medicine","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Primary Care","Diagnosis","Patient Communication","EMR","Prescribing"],"reqs":["Medical degree (MD/MBBS) and active DHA license (or DHA eligibility letter) as a General Practitioner.","2+ years o