iage flow, coordinate rapid cath-lab/stroke/OR activations, and ensure safe disposition decisions.\n- Supervise and teach junior medical officers, rotating residents, and emergency nursing teams on shift.\n- Maintain thorough medicolegal documentation and participate in ED morbidity & mortality reviews.\n\nRequirements:\n- Medical degree plus Board Certification in Emergency Medicine (ABEM, FRCEM, Arab Board, or DHA Tier-1 equivalent).\n- Current ACLS, ATLS, and PALS certifications.\n- 5+ years of attending-level experience in a high-volume emergency department.\n- Decisive clinical leadership under acute pressure.\n\nNice to have:\n- Point-of-Care Ultrasound (POCUS) fellowship or credentialing.\n- Arabic and English fluency.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $5,500–$8,500 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- VIP family medical insurance, malpractice coverage, and DHA license fee reimbursement\n- 30 calendar days paid annual leave plus annual return flight allowance\n- Dedicated paid CME leave (7 days/year) and conference grant\n- Relocation package and housing support for international physicians\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Credential, degree, and active clinical license verification\n- 2. 45-minute clinical case discussion with the department lead\n- 3. Facility tour, schedule alignment, and Medical Director sign-off","field":"Medicine","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Emergency Medicine","Trauma Care","ACLS","Triage","Critical Care"],"reqs":["Medical degree plus Board Certification in Emergency Medicine (ABEM, FRCEM, Arab Board, or DHA Tier-1 equivalent).","Current ACLS, ATLS, and PALS certifications.","5+ years of attending-level experience in a high-volume emergency department.","Decisive clinical leadership under acute pressure."],"lo":5500,"hi":8500,"days":16,"hours":1},{"company":"Aurora Medical Center","title":"Radiologist","description":"Aurora Medical Center is a 400-bed JCI-accredited tea