st-board experience managing high-risk obstetrics and gynecologic surgery.\n- Compassionate bedside manner and strong multidisciplinary teamwork.\n\nNice to have:\n- Advanced training in minimally invasive/laparoscopic surgery or fetal medicine.\n- Fluency in Arabic and English.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $5,500–$8,800 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- VIP family medical insurance, malpractice coverage, and DHA license fee reimbursement\n- 30 calendar days paid annual leave plus annual return flight allowance\n- Dedicated paid CME leave (7 days/year) and conference grant\n- Relocation package and housing support for international physicians\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Credential, degree, and active clinical license verification\n- 2. 45-minute clinical case discussion with the department lead\n- 3. Facility tour, schedule alignment, and Medical Director sign-off","field":"Medicine","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Obstetrics","Gynecology","Ultrasound","Surgery","Patient Care"],"reqs":["Medical degree plus Board Certification in Obstetrics & Gynecology (MRCOG, ABOG, Arab Board, or equivalent).","Active DHA Specialist/Consultant OB-GYN license (or eligibility).","4+ years of independent post-board experience managing high-risk obstetrics and gynecologic surgery.","Compassionate bedside manner and strong multidisciplinary teamwork."],"lo":5500,"hi":8800,"days":9,"hours":11},{"company":"Aurora Medical Center","title":"Dentist","description":"Aurora Medical Center is a 400-bed JCI-accredited teaching hospital and multi-specialty outpatient network in Dubai serving over 450,000 patient visits annually. We combine academic clinical rigor, subspecialty surgery, and modern diagnostic imaging under one campus. We're hiring a Dentist to join the team (on-site, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nDeliver calm, conservative restorative, preventive, and minor oral-surgical dental care inside Aurora's integrated hospital dental suite in Dubai.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Perform comprehensive oral examinations, digital radiographic diagnostics, and individualized treatment planning.\n- Deliver high-craft composite restorations, root canal treatments, crowns/bridges, and uncomplicated extractions.\n- Collaborate with Aurora's periodontists, orthodontists, and maxillofacial surgeons on complex cases.\n- Explain treatment options, preventive hygiene, and transparent pricing clearly to patients.\n- Uphold strict sterilization, infection-control, and clinical charting standards.\n\nRequirements:\n- BDS / DDS / DMD degree and an active DHA General Dentist license (or eligibility).\n- 2+ years of post-internship clinical dental practice.\n- Strong restorative and endodontic proficiency with gentle chairside communication.\n- Fluency in English; Arabic is an advantage.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience with CAD/CAM digital impressions (iTero/CEREC) or cosmetic dentistry.\n- Prior clinic experience in the UAE.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,800–$4,600 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- VIP family medical insurance, malpractice coverage, and DHA license fee reimbursement\n- 30 calendar days paid annual leave plus annual return flight allowance\n- Dedicated paid CME leave (7 days/year) and conference grant\n- Relocation package and housing support for international physicians\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Credential, degree, and active clinical license verification\n- 2. 45-minute clinical case discussion with the department lead\n- 3. Facility tour, schedule alignment, and Medical Director sign-off","field":"Medicine","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Dentistry","Restorative Dentistry","Oral Surgery","Patient Care","Radiography"],"reqs":["BDS / DDS / DMD degree and an active DHA General Dentist license (or eligibility).","2+ years of post-internship clinical dental practice.","Strong restorative and endodontic proficien