e family\n- Protected academic teaching time and paid annual medical conference support\n- Medical malpractice protection and transparent on-call compensation\n- 22 days paid annual leave plus public holidays\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Credential, degree, and active clinical license verification\n- 2. 45-minute clinical case discussion with the department lead\n- 3. Facility tour, schedule alignment, and Medical Director sign-off","field":"Medicine","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["Internal Medicine","Clinical Rounds","Diagnosis","EMR","Teamwork"],"reqs":["Doctor of Medicine (MD) degree from an accredited medical school and Lebanese Colloquium / license eligibility.","Strong foundational clinical knowledge across internal medicine, cardiology, and acute care.","Resilience, intellectual honesty, and collaborative teamwork on inpatient call schedules.","Fluent Arabic and English (French helpful)."],"lo":1100,"hi":1700,"days":2,"hours":21},{"company":"Cedarcrest Hospital","title":"Cardiologist","description":"Cedarcrest Hospital is a 350-bed university teaching hospital in Beirut recognized regionally for tertiary cardiology, critical care, emergency medicine, and clinical residency training. Over 1,200 physicians, nurses, and allied health professionals deliver evidence-based inpatient and outpatient care. We're hiring a Cardiologist to join the team (on-site, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nDirect Cedarcrest's adult cardiology service in Beirut—combining interventional cath-lab leadership, complex echocardiography, outpatient clinics, and fellowship teaching.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Lead clinical care across inpatient cardiology, CCU consultations, and high-volume outpatient heart clinics.\n- Perform diagnostic coronary angiographies, PCI interventions, and transesophageal/stress echocardiography.\n- Lead acute STEMI on-call pathways alongside emergency medicine and cardiothoracic surgery teams.\n- Ment