esiologist","description":"Cedarcrest Hospital is a 350-bed university teaching hospital in Beirut recognized regionally for tertiary cardiology, critical care, emergency medicine, and clinical residency training. Over 1,200 physicians, nurses, and allied health professionals deliver evidence-based inpatient and outpatient care. We're hiring an Anesthesiologist to join the team (on-site, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nProvide safe perioperative anesthesia across 12 operating suites—covering cardiac, orthopedic, obstetric, and laparoscopic surgery plus ICU airway/pain support in Beirut.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Conduct thorough pre-anesthetic patient evaluations, risk stratification, and airway planning.\n- Administer general, regional (ultrasound-guided nerve blocks), and neuraxial anesthesia safely across surgical suites.\n- Manage intraoperative hemodynamics, blood conservation, and acute perioperative emergencies.\n- Oversee post-anesthesia care unit (PACU) recovery and acute post-operative pain protocols.\n- Provide backup airway and critical-care support to the surgical ICU and labor ward.\n\nRequirements:\n- Medical degree plus Board Certification / Specialty Diploma in Anesthesiology & Reanimation.\n- Active Lebanese Order of Physicians specialist registration and 4+ years independent OR practice.\n- Strong command of ultrasound-guided regional blocks and difficult airway management.\n- Calm situational awareness and clear OR team communication.\n\nNice to have:\n- Subspecialty experience in cardiothoracic or obstetric anesthesia.\n- Trilingual Arabic, English, and French.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $4,500–$7,000 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Full hospital medical coverage for staff and immediate family\n- Protected academic teaching time and paid annual medical conference support\n- Medical malpractice protection and transparent on-call compensation\n- 22 days paid annual leave plus public holidays\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Credential, degree, and active clinical license verification\n- 2. 45-minute clinical case discussion with the department lead\n- 3. Facility tour, schedule alignment, and Medical Director sign-off","field":"Medicine","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["Anesthesiology","Airway Management","Pain Management","Critical Care","Patient Safety"],"reqs":["Medical degree plus Board Certification / Specialty Diploma in Anesthesiology & Reanimation.","Active Lebanese Order of Physicians specialist registration and 4+ years independent OR practice.","Strong command of ultrasound-guided regional blocks and difficult airway management.","Calm situational awareness and clear OR team communication."],"lo":4500,"hi":7000,"days":16,"hours":7},{"company":"Cedarcrest Hospital","title":"Psychiatrist","description":"Cedarcrest Hospital is a 350-bed university teaching hospital in Beirut recognized regionally for tertiary cardiology, critical care, emergency medicine, and clinical residency training. Over 1,200 physicians, nurses, and allied health professionals deliver evidence-based inpatient and outpatient care. We're hiring a Psychiatrist to join the team (hybrid, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nDeliver thoughtful outpatient psychiatric assessments, evidence-based psychopharmacology, and hybrid telehealth follow-ups (20–24 hrs/week) within Cedarcrest's behavioral health unit.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Conduct comprehensive psychiatric evaluations for adults experiencing mood, anxiety, trauma, and stress disorders.\n- Develop individualized treatment plans combining safe psychopharmacology with psychotherapeutic support.\n- Run structured telehealth follow-up clinics alongside in-person hospital outpatient hours.\n- Collaborate weekly in multidisciplinary case reviews with clinical psychologists and medical social workers.\n- Provide consultation-liaison psychiatric input for medical/surgical inpatients when requested.\n\nRequirements:\n- Medical degree plus Board Certification / Specialty Diploma in Psychiatry.\n- Active specialist license and 3+ years of independent outpatient psychiatric experience.\n- Fluent Arabic and English with trauma-informed, non-judgmental clinical presence.\n- Comfort conducting structured clinical telehealth sessions securely.\n\nNice to have:\n- Training in CBT, ACT, or consultation-liaison psychiatry.\n- French language proficiency.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,200–$3,600 USD / month (Part-time, Hybrid)\n- Full hospital medical coverage for staff and immediate family\n- Protected academic teaching time and paid annual medical conference support\n- Medical malpractice protection and transparent on-call compensation\n- 22 days paid annual leave plus public holidays\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Credential, degree, and active clinical license verification\n- 2. 45-minute clinical case discussion with the department lead\n- 3. Facility tour, schedule alignment, and Medical Director sign-off","field":"Medicine","seniority":"senior","type":"part_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["Psychiatry","Mental Health Assessment","Psychopharmacology","Therapy","Telehealth"],"reqs":["Medical degree plus Board Certification / Specialty Diploma in Psychiatry.","Active specialist license and 3+ years of independent outpatient psychiatric experience.","Fluent Arabic and English with trauma-informed, non-judgmental clinical presence.","Comfort conducting structured clinical telehealth sessions securely."],"lo":2200,"hi":3600,"days":2,"hours":12},{"company":"Cedarcrest Hospital","title":"Medical Intern","description":"Cedarcrest Hospital is a 350-bed university teaching hospital in Beirut recognized regionally for tertiary cardiology, critical care, emergency medicine, and clinical residency training. Over 1,200 physicians, nurses, and allied health professionals deliver evidence-based inpatient and outpatient care. We're hiring a Medical Intern to join the team (on-site, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nA structured 12-month rotating clinical internship in Beirut across Internal Medicine, General Surgery, Pediatrics, and Emergency Medicine.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Rotate through core hospital departments under direct supervision of senior residents and attending physicians.\n- Take thorough patient histories, perform supervised physical exams, and track daily vitals and lab results.\n- Practice basic clinical skills (IV cannulation, ECG acquisition, wound care) safely with nursing and resident mentors.\n- Join daily teaching rounds and weekly clinical case presentations.\n\nRequirements:\n- Final-year medical student or recent MD/MBBS graduate eligible for hospital internship training.\n- Solid preclinical and clinical clerkship foundation and valid BLS certification.\n- Strong work ethic, humility, and compassionate bedside attitude.\n- Fluent Arabic and English.\n\nNice to have:\n- Prior student clinical electives or volunteer triage experience.\n- French comprehension for reviewing bilingual medical notes.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $450–$750 USD / month (Internship, On-site)\n- Full hospital medical coverage for staff and immediate family\n- Protected academic teaching time and paid annual medical conference support\n- Medical malpractice protection and transparent on-call compensation\n- 22 days paid annual leave plus public holidays\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Application & portfolio/CV review (2–3 business days)\n- 2. 30-minute conversation with your team mentor — focused on projects and curiosity, no trick questions\n- 3. Final placement confirmation and start-date onboarding","field":"Medicine","seniority":"intern","type":"internship","mode":"onsite","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["Clinical Rounds","Patient History","Teamwork","EMR"],"reqs":["Final-year medical student or recent MD/MBBS graduate eligible for hospital internship training.","Solid preclinical and clinical clerkship foundation and valid BLS certification.","Strong work ethic, humility, and compassionate bedside attitude.","Fluent Arabic and English."],"lo":450,"hi":750,"days":9,"hours":17},{"company":"Cedarcrest Hospital","title":"ICU Nurse","description":"Cedarcrest Hospital is a 350-bed university teaching hospital in Beirut recognized regionally for tertiary cardiology, critical care, emergency medicine, and clinical residency training. Over 1,200 physicians, nurses, and allied health professionals deliver evidence-based inpatient and outpatient care. We're hiring an ICU Nurse to join the team (on-site, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nDeliver vigilant 1:1 and 1:2 bedside nursing care in Cedarcrest's 24-bed Medical-Surgical and Cardiac Intensive Care Unit in Beirut.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Monitor critically ill patients continuously—managing invasive arterial/CVP lines, telemetry, and sedation scales.\n- Manage mechanical ventilators, titrate vasoactive infusions safely, and coordinate weaning trials with intensivists.\n- Perform rapid emergency responses, code-blue support, and meticulous infection-prevention bundles.\n- Update anxious families empathetically during visiting hours and physician updates.\n- Document hourly ICU flowsheets accurately in the hospital EMR.\n\nRequirements:\n- BSN degree and active Lebanese nursing practice license.\n- 2+ years of hands-on nursing experience in an adult ICU, CCU, or high-dependency unit.\n- Current BLS and ACLS certifications.\n- Fluent Arabic and English with calm precision in high-acuity moments.\n\nNice to have:\n- CCRN or post-graduate critical care nursing certificate.\n- Experience managing CRRT dialysis or post-cardiac-surgery patients.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,300–$2,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Full hospital medical coverage for staff and immediate family\n- Protected academic teaching time and paid annual medical conference support\n- Medical malpractice protection and transparent on-call compensation\n- 22 days paid annual leave plus public holidays\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Credential, degree, and active clinical license verification\n- 2. 45-minute clinical case discussion with the department lead\n- 3. Facility tour, schedule alignment, and Medical Director sign-off","field":"Healthcare","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["Critical Care","Patient Care","Ventilator Management","Medication Administration","EMR"],"reqs":["BSN degree and active Lebanese nursing practice license.","2+ years of hands-on nursing experience in an adult ICU, CCU, or high-dependency unit.","Current BLS and ACLS certifications.","Fluent Arabic and English with calm precision in high-acuity moments."],"lo":1300,"hi":2300,"days":16,"hours":22},{"company":"Aurora Medical Center","title":"Nutritionist","description":"Aurora Medical Center is a 400-bed JCI-accredited teaching hospital and multi-specialty outpatient network in Dubai serving over 450,000 patient visits annually. We combine academic clinical rigor, subspecialty surgery, and modern diagnostic imaging under one campus. We're hiring a Nutritionist to join the team (on-site, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nProvide clinical medical nutrition therapy for hospitalized patients and run outpatient metabolic, bariatric, and sports-nutrition counseling at Aurora in Dubai.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Conduct inpatient nutritional risk screenings and tailor therapeutic enteral/oral meal plans with culinary teams.\n- Run outpatient consultations for diabetes, PCOS, cardiovascular health, and sustainable weight management.\n- Track body composition, lab biomarkers, and realistic behavioral goals across follow-up visits.\n- Lead monthly community wellness talks and corporate preventive-health workshops.\n- Collaborate with endocrinologists, cardiologists, and gastroenterologists on shared care plans.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's or Master's degree in Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics.\n- Active DHA Clinical Dietitian / Nutritionist license (or eligibility) and 2+ years clinical experience.\n- Evidence-based counseling style free of fad-diet messaging.\n- Fluent English; Arabic is a strong advantage.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience with inpatient ICU/oncology enteral nutrition protocols.\n- Certified Diabetes Educator (CDE) credential.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- VIP family medical insurance, malpractice coverage, and DHA license fee reimbursement\n- 30 calendar days paid annual leave plus annual return flight allowance\n- Dedicated paid CME leave (7 days/year) and conference grant\n- Relocation package and housing support for international physicians\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Credential, degree, and active clinical license verification\n- 2. 45-minute clinical case discussion with the department lead\n- 3. Facility tour, schedule alignment, and Medical Director sign-off","field":"Healthcare","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Nutrition","Diet Planning","Patient Counseling","Health Education"],"reqs":["Bachelor's or Master's degree in Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics.","Active DHA Clinical Dietitian / Nutritionist license (or eligibility) and 2+ years clinical experience.","Evidence-based counseling style free of fad-diet messaging.","Fluent English; Arabic is a strong advantage."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":2,"hours":3},{"company":"Aurora Medical Center","title":"Biomedical Engineer","description":"Aurora Medical Center is a 400-bed JCI-accredited teaching hospital and multi-specialty outpatient network in Dubai serving over 450,000 patient visits annually. We combine academic clinical rigor, subspecialty surgery, and modern diagnostic imaging under one campus. We're hiring a Biomedical Engineer to join the team (on-site, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nKeep Aurora's 1,800+ clinical devices—MRI/CT scanners, ICU ventilators, anesthesia machines, and infusion pumps—calibrated, safe, and JCI audit-ready.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Execute scheduled preventive maintenance (PM) and electrical safety testing across critical-care and diagnostic assets.\n- Respond promptly to clinical department trouble calls to diagnose and repair medical equipment faults.\n- Manage OEM service contracts, spare-parts inventory, and warranty escalations for imaging and lab analyzers.\n- Lead pre-purchase technical evaluations and acceptance testing for newly acquired medical devices.\n- Maintain spotless CMMS calibration and JCI compliance logs.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's degree in Biomedical Engineering or Clinical Engineering.\n- 2+ years of hands-on hospital biomedical engineering experience.\n- Solid troubleshooting skills across patient monitors, ventilators, and infusion/OR equipment.\n- Strong knowledge of IEC 60601 safety testing and JCI/MOHAP hospital compliance.\n\nNice to have:\n- OEM training certificates (GE, Philips, Dräger, or Mindray).\n- Experience managing hospital CMMS databases.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- VIP family medical insurance, malpractice coverage, and DHA license fee reimbursement\n- 30 calendar days paid annual leave plus annual return flight allowance\n- Dedicated paid CME leave (7 days/year) and conference grant\n- Relocation package and housing support for international physicians\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Engineering","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Biomedical Engineering","Medical Equipment","Maintenance","Troubleshooting","Regulatory Compliance"],"reqs":["Bachelor's degree in Biomedical Engineering or Clinical Engineering.","2+ years of hands-on hospital biomedical engineering experience.","Solid troubleshooting skills across patient monitors, ventilators, and infusion/OR equipment.","Strong knowledge of IEC 60601 safety testing and JCI/MOHAP hospital compliance."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":9,"hours":8},{"company":"Summit Bank","title":"Relationship Manager (SME Banking)","description":"Summit Bank is a UK retail, SME, and commercial bank serving 1.4 million personal and business customers through modern digital channels and regional relationship hubs. Our London teams balance prudent credit underwriting with fast, transparent business lending. We're hiring a Relationship Manager (SME Banking) to join the team (on-site, London, UK).\n\nAbout the role:\nManage and grow a portfolio of 45 UK SME clients (£2M–£25M turnover)—structuring working-capital facilities, term loans, and treasury services from London.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Act as primary trusted advisor to SME founders and finance directors across your London portfolio.\n- Analyze historical financials, cash-flow forecasts, and collateral to structure responsible credit proposals.\n- Present well-reasoned credit memos to the Credit Committee and negotiate facility covenants cleanly.\n- Identify cross-sell opportunities across FX hedging, merchant acquiring, and asset finance.\n- Monitor portfolio early-warning indicators and conduct annual facility reviews on time.\n\nRequirements:\n- 3+ years in UK commercial or SME relationship banking with credit-writing responsibility.\n- Strong ability to interpret P&L, balance sheet, cash-flow statements, and debt-service coverage ratios.\n- Consultative business development instincts paired with sound credit risk judgment.\n- Clear written and interpersonal presence with business owners.\n\nNice to have:\n- LIBF / ACIB / Chartered Banker qualification.\n- Existing network across London or South East UK SMEs.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- 27 days annual leave (plus UK bank holidays) and hybrid City of London office model\n- Non-contributory 10% employer pension contribution and private healthcare\n- Annual discretionary performance bonus and preferential staff banking rates\n- Paid study support for CFA, LIBF, or FRM qualifications\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Banking","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"London, UK","skills":["Relationship Management","Credit Analysis","Sales","Financial Statements","Communication"],"reqs":["3+ years in UK commercial or SME relationship banking with credit-writing responsibility.","Strong ability to interpret P&L, balance sheet, cash-flow statements, and debt-service coverage ratios.","Consultative business development instincts paired with sound credit risk judgment.","Clear written and interpersonal presence with business owners."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":16,"hours":13},{"company":"Summit Bank","title":"Credit Risk Analyst","description":"Summit Bank is a UK retail, SME, and commercial bank serving 1.4 million personal and business customers through modern digital channels and regional relationship hubs. Our London teams balance prudent credit underwriting with fast, transparent business lending. We're hiring a Credit Risk Analyst to join the team (hybrid, London, UK).\n\nAbout the role:\nEvaluate corporate and SME lending risk across Summit Bank's £1.8B loan book—combining transaction-level credit underwriting reviews with SQL portfolio stress testing.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Assess new commercial credit applications and annual reviews, challenging financial assumptions rigorously.\n- Query loan-book performance data in SQL and Excel to track delinquency, PD/LGD migration, and sector concentration.\n- Support IFRS 9 expected credit loss (ECL) provisioning and Basel III capital reporting.\n- Prepare monthly risk-appetite dashboards and stress-test summaries for the Credit Risk Committee.\n- Partner with Relationship Managers to refine sector underwriting guidelines.\n\nRequirements:\n- 2+ years in credit risk, corporate underwriting, or portfolio risk analytics at a bank or lender.\n- Strong financial statement analysis and Excel/SQL modeling skills.\n- Working understanding of credit risk metrics (PD, LGD, EAD), IFRS 9, and UK banking regulation.\n- Structured, objective analytical writing.\n\nNice to have:\n- Python or SAS/R experience for scorecard monitoring.\n- Progress toward CFA or FRM.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- 27 days annual leave (plus UK bank holidays) and hybrid City of London office model\n- Non-contributory 10% employer pension contribution and private healthcare\n- Annual discretionary performance bonus and preferential staff banking rates\n- Paid study support for CFA, LIBF, or FRM qualifications\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Banking","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"London, UK","skills":["Credit Risk","Financial Analysis","Excel","SQL","Basel III"],"reqs":["2+ years in credit risk, corporate underwriting, or portfolio risk analytics at a bank or lender.","Strong financial statement analysis and Excel/SQL modeling skills.","Working understanding of credit risk metrics (PD, LGD, EAD), IFRS 9, and UK banking regulation.","Structured, objective analytical writing."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":2,"hours":18},{"company":"Summit Bank","title":"Treasury Analyst","description":"Summit Bank is a UK retail, SME, and commercial 