rsation","field":"Banking","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"London, UK","skills":["Treasury","Liquidity Management","Excel","Bloomberg","Financial Modeling"],"reqs":["Bachelor's degree in Finance, Economics, Mathematics, or Accounting.","2+ years in bank treasury, ALM, or corporate liquidity management.","Strong Excel modeling skills and familiarity with Bloomberg or Refinitiv.","High precision under morning market cut-off deadlines."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":9,"hours":23},{"company":"Summit Bank","title":"Graduate Banking Trainee","description":"Summit Bank is a UK retail, SME, and commercial bank serving 1.4 million personal and business customers through modern digital channels and regional relationship hubs. Our London teams balance prudent credit underwriting with fast, transparent business lending. We're hiring a Graduate Banking Trainee to join the team (on-site, London, UK).\n\nAbout the role:\nA 6-month rotational London trainee program spanning Commercial Banking, Credit Risk, and Treasury—designed as a launchpad into full-time analyst roles.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Complete two 3-month rotations across SME Banking, Credit Risk, or Treasury Operations.\n- Support analysts with company research, financial spreadsheet spreads, and portfolio data checks.\n- Shadow client meetings and credit committee discussions to see real banking decisions firsthand.\n- Deliver an end-of-program capstone analysis to senior UK banking leaders.\n\nRequirements:\n- Recent graduate (or final-year student) in Finance, Economics, Business, Accounting, or a quantitative discipline.\n- Strong numerical fluency, comfort with Excel, and curiosity about commercial banking.\n- Clear written and spoken English and collaborative team spirit.\n- Eligible to work on-site in London.\n\nNice to have:\n- University finance society leadership or prior summer internship.\n- Basic familiarity with financial statements or SQL.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $450–$800 USD / month (Internship, On-site)\n- 27 days annual leave (plus UK bank holidays) and hybrid City of London office model\n- Non-contributory 10% employer pension contribution and private healthcare\n- Annual discretionary performance bonus and preferential staff banking rates\n- Paid study support for CFA, LIBF, or FRM qualifications\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Application & portfolio/CV review (2–3 business days)\n- 2. 30-minute conversation with your team mentor — focused on projects and curiosity, no trick questions\n- 3. Final placement confirmation and start-date onboarding","field":"Banking","seniority":"intern","type":"internship","mode":"onsite","location":"London, UK","skills":["Excel","Communication","Financial Analysis","Teamwork"],"reqs":["Recent graduate (or final-year student) in Finance, Economics, Business, Accounting, or a quantitative discipline.","Strong numerical fluency, comfort with Excel, and curiosity about commercial banking.","Clear written and spoken English and collaborative team spirit.","Eligible to work on-site in London."],"lo":450,"hi":800,"days":16,"hours":4},{"company":"Summit Bank","title":"Economic Research Analyst","description":"Summit Bank is a UK retail, SME, and commercial bank serving 1.4 million personal and business customers through modern digital channels and regional relationship hubs. Our London teams balance prudent credit underwriting with fast, transparent business lending. We're hiring an Economic Research Analyst to join the team (hybrid, London, UK).\n\nAbout the role:\nProduce clear, data-backed UK and global macroeconomic research that helps Summit's bankers, treasury desk, and SME clients navigate inflation, rates, and trade shifts.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Author Summit Bank's monthly UK Economic Outlook and rapid-response notes on BoE rate and CPI releases.\n- Build and maintain time-series forecasting models in Python/Excel for GDP, inflation, housing, and gilt yields.\n- Analyze regional UK sector trends (manufacturing, hospitality, retail) affecting our SME loan book.\n- Present macro briefings clearly to internal relationship teams and client roundtables.\n- Automate public data ingestion from ONS, Bank of England, and Eurostat.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's or Master's degree in Economics or Econometrics.\n- 2+ years in macroeconomic research, financial markets economics, or policy analysis.\n- Strong time-series econometrics, Python/R or EViews proficiency, and crisp non-academic writing.\n- Ability to explain nuanced economic signals plainly to business clients.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience using Bloomberg/Macrobond APIs.\n- Published market commentary or blog samples.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- 27 days annual leave (plus UK bank holidays) and hybrid City of London office model\n- Non-contributory 10% employer pension contribution and private healthcare\n- Annual discretionary performance bonus and preferential staff banking rates\n- Paid study support for CFA, LIBF, or FRM qualifications\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Economics","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"London, UK","skills":["Economics","Forecasting","Excel","Python","Report Writing"],"reqs":["Bachelor's or Master's degree in Economics or Econometrics.","2+ years in macroeconomic research, financial markets economics, or policy analysis.","Strong time-series econometrics, Python/R or EViews proficiency, and crisp non-academic writing.","Ability to explain nuanced economic signals plainly to business clients."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":2,"hours":9},{"company":"Levant Commercial Bank","title":"Bank Teller","description":"Levant Commercial Bank is an established commercial and retail bank operating 40 branches alongside a rapidly growing mobile banking and merchant treasury platform. We focus on transparent customer service, rigorous AML governance, and SME trade financing. We're hiring a Bank Teller to join the team (on-site, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nDeliver fast, accurate, and courteous branch counter service in Beirut—handling cash transactions, transfers, card pickups, and frontline KYC checks.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Process cash deposits, withdrawals, check clearing, and domestic/international wire requests accurately.\n- Verify customer identification, signatures, and basic KYC documentation on every transaction.\n- Balance daily teller cash drawers to zero discrepancy at branch close.\n- Spot unusual transaction requests and escalate potential fraud or AML red flags promptly.\n- Guide customers smoothly toward digital mobile-banking self-service features where helpful.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's degree in Business, Finance, Banking, or Accounting (or equivalent diploma with branch experience).\n- Fluent Arabic and English (French is a plus).\n- High numerical accuracy, integrity, and calm patience during peak branch hours.\n- Clear customer-first communication.\n\nNice to have:\n- 1+ year in retail banking, cashiering, or customer service.\n- Familiarity with core banking teller systems.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $700–$1,200 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive NSSF + private Class-A family medical insurance\n- Transportation allowance, school tuition support, and 18–22 days paid leave\n- Structured banking compliance and leadership training pathways\n- Preferential employee banking and credit facilities\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Banking","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["Customer Service","Cash Handling","Banking Operations","Attention to Detail","Arabic"],"reqs":["Bachelor's degree in Business, Finance, Banking, or Accounting (or equivalent diploma with branch experience).","Fluent Arabic and English (French is a plus).","High numerical accuracy, integrity, and calm patience during peak branch hours.","Clear customer-first communication."],"lo":700,"hi":1200,"days":9,"hours":14},{"company":"Levant Commercial Bank","title":"Loan Officer","description":"Levant Commercial Bank is an established commercial and retail bank operating 40 branches alongside a rapidly growing mobile banking and merchant treasury platform. We focus on transparent customer service, rigorous AML governance, and SME trade financing. We're hiring a Loan Officer to join the team (on-site, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nGuide personal and micro-business clients through responsible loan products—assessing repayment capacity, verifying documentation, and meeting branch lending standards.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Consult with retail and small-business applicants to match them with transparent, suitable credit facilities.\n- Review income proofs, bank statements, credit bureau reports, and collateral documents thoroughly.\n- Calculate debt-burden ratios and prepare complete underwriting files for credit approval.\n- Explain interest rates, fee schedules, and repayment terms clearly with zero hidden surprises.\n- Follow up proactively on early-stage arrears and maintain branch compliance audit readiness.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's degree in Finance, Economics, or Business Administration.\n- 2+ years in retail lending, microfinance, or credit underwriting at a bank.\n- Solid understanding of personal/SME credit assessment and central bank lending rules.\n- Fluent Arabic and English with strong ethics and interpersonal warmth.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience originating auto, housing, or SME working-capital loans.\n- Strong local market network.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,300–$2,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive NSSF + private Class-A family medical insurance\n- Transportation allowance, school tuition support, and 18–22 days paid leave\n- Structured banking compliance and leadership training pathways\n- Preferential employee banking and credit facilities\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Banking","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["Lending","Credit Analysis","Customer Service","Compliance","Sales"],"reqs":["Bachelor's degree in Finance, Economics, or Business Administration.","2+ years in retail lending, microfinance, or credit underwriting at a bank.","Solid understanding of personal/SME credit assessment and central bank lending rules.","Fluent Arabic and English with strong ethics and interpersonal warmth."],"lo":1300,"hi":2300,"days":16,"hours":19},{"company":"Levant Commercial Bank","title":"AML Compliance Officer","description":"Levant Commercial Bank is an established commercial and retail bank operating 40 branches alongside a rapidly growing mobile banking and merchant treasury platform. We focus on transparent customer service, rigorous AML governance, and SME trade financing. We're hiring an AML Compliance Officer to join the team (on-site, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nLead complex financial-crime investigations, enhanced due diligence (EDD) reviews, and regulatory SIC/Central Bank reporting across Levant Commercial Bank's Beirut headquarters.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Lead end-to-end investigations into escalated transaction-monitoring alerts, PEP matches, and sanctions hits.\n- Draft high-quality Suspicious Transaction Reports (STRs) for the Special Investigation Commission (SIC).\n- Review and approve high-risk corporate/correspondent banking KYC/EDD onboarding files.\n- Update internal AML/CFT policies, screening rules, and annual bank-wide staff training.\n- Serve as key liaison during internal audits and correspondent-bank compliance due diligence reviews.\n\nRequirements:\n- 5+ years in banking AML/CFT compliance, transaction monitoring, or financial-crime investigations.\n- Deep mastery of FATF standards, KYC/EDD best practices, and correspondent-banking expectations.\n- Fluent Arabic and English with sharp investigative writing.\n- High personal integrity and decisive analytical judgment.\n\nNice to have:\n- CAMS (Certified Anti-Money Laundering Specialist) or ICA Diploma.\n- Experience tuning Actimize, Fircosoft, or SAS AML scenarios.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,400–$3,800 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive NSSF + private Class-A family medical insurance\n- Transportation allowance, school tuition support, and 18–22 days paid leave\n- Structured banking compliance and leadership training pathways\n- Preferential employee banking and credit facilities\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Banking","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["AML","KYC","Compliance","Investigations","Reporting"],"reqs":["5+ years in banking AML/CFT compliance, transaction monitoring, or financial-crime investigations.","Deep mastery of FATF standards, KYC/EDD best practices, and correspondent-banking expectations.","Fluent Arabic and English with sharp investigative writing.","High personal integrity and decisive analytical judgment."],"lo":2400,"hi":3800,"days":2,"hours":0},{"company":"Levant Commercial Bank","title":"Branch Manager","description":"Levant Commercial Bank is an established commercial and retail bank operating 40 branches alongside a rapidly growing mobile banking and merchant treasury platform. We focus on transparent customer service, rigorous AML governance, and SME trade financing. We're hiring a Branch Manager to join the team (on-site, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nLead a 12-person full-service Beirut branch—driving healthy deposit and SME client growth while upholding spotless operational controls and service quality.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Manage, coach, and appraise a 12-person team of tellers, customer service officers, and loan officers.\n- Grow branch deposits, payroll accounts, and quality SME/retail relationships in the local catchment area.\n- Oversee daily vault controls, dual-custody cash procedures, and branch audit readiness.\n- Resolve escalated customer complaints quickly and maintain top-quartile service wait times.\n- Report monthly commercial pipeline, risk, and operational metrics to Regional Management.\n\nRequirements:\n- 7+ years in commercial/retail banking, including 2+ years as Branch Manager or Assistant Branch Manager.\n- Strong command of branch operations, cash controls, AML/KYC compliance, and commercial sales.\n- Proven leadership motivating branch staff and cultivating loyal local business relationships.\n- Fluent Arabic and English (French advantageous).\n\nNice to have:\n- Track record turning around underperforming branches or launching digital-first branch models.\n- Bachelor's or Master's in Finance/Banking.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,400–$3,800 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive NSSF + private Class-A family medical insurance\n- Transportation allowance, school tuition support, and 18–22 days paid leave\n- Structured banking compliance and leadership training pathways\n- Preferential employee banking and credit facilities\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Banking","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["Team Leadership","Banking Operations","Sales","Customer Service","Compliance"],"reqs":["7+ years in commercial/retail banking, including 2+ years as Branch Manager or Assistant Branch Manager.","Strong command of branch operations, cash controls, AML/KYC compliance, and commercial sales.","Proven leadership motivating branch staff and cultivating loyal local business relationships.","Fluent Arabic and English (French advantageous)."],"lo":2400,"hi":3800,"days":9,"hours":5},{"company":"Gulfstream Capital","title":"Investment Analyst","description":"Gulfstream Capital is a DIFC-regulated asset management firm overseeing $3.8B across MENA public equities, sovereign/corporate fixed income, and quantitative multi-asset strategies for institutional and family-office clients. We're hiring an Investment Analyst to join the team (on-site, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nCover listed MENA consumer, industrial, and financial equities—building bottom-up DCF/comps models, meeting management teams, and pitching conviction ideas to Portfolio Managers.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Build and maintain detailed 3-statement financial models, DCF valuations, and peer multiples in Excel.\n- Analyze quarterly earnings releases, sector regulatory shifts, and competitive moats across GCC/MENA stocks.\n- Attend management meetings, investor conferences, and site visits to validate thesis assumptions.\n- Write concise, thesis-driven investment memos clearly highlighting upside drivers and downside risks.\n- Track consensus estimates and catalyst calendars in Bloomberg and internal research tools.\n\nRequirements:\n- 2+ years in buy-side equity research, sell-side research, or investment banking.\n- Expert financial modeling and accounting fluency (IFRS, ROIC, working capital, valuation).\n- Hands-on command of Bloomberg Terminal / Capital IQ.\n- Strong intellectual honesty and persuasive written investment communication.\n\nNice to have:\n- CFA Charterholder or CFA Level II/III candidate.\n- Prior coverage of MENA/EM equities and Arabic fluency.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- DIFC-grade family medical coverage, life insurance, and annual flight ticket\n- 25 days paid annual leave plus performance-linked annual bonus\n- Full sponsorship for CFA, CAIA, or CQF study materials and exam fees\n- Modern DIFC office with Bloomberg terminals and research library\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Banking","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Financial Modeling","Valuation","Excel","Equity Research","Bloomberg"],"reqs":["2+ years in buy-side equity research, sell-side research, or investment banking.","Expert financial modeling and accounting fluency (IFRS, ROIC, working capital, valuation).","Hands-on command of Bloomberg Terminal / Capital IQ.","Strong intellectual honesty and persuasive written investment communication."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":16,"hours":10},{"company":"Gulfstream Capital","title":"Portfolio Manager","description":"Gulfstream Capital is a DIFC-regulated asset management firm overseeing $3.8B across MENA public equities, sovereign/corporate fixed income, and quantitative multi-asset strategies for institutional and family-office clients. We're hiring a Portfolio Manager to join the team (on-site, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nCo-manage Gulfstream's flagship $900M MENA Active Equity mandate in DIFC—owning portfolio construction, factor/risk sizing, analyst mentoring, and institutional LP updates.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Drive security selection, position sizing, and sector allocation decisions across our flagship regional equity fund.\n- Monitor portfolio risk exposures (beta, liquidity, factor tilts, currency, drawdown budgets) daily.\n- Lead weekly investment committee debates, challenging analyst theses constructively.\n- Present quarterly attribution, market outlook, and strategy reviews to sovereign and family-office investors.\n- Ensure strict adherence to DFSA fund mandates, best-execution, and compliance guidelines.\n\nRequirements:\n- 10+ years in institutional public-equity investment management with verifiable track record.\n- CFA Charterholder (mandatory or equivalent senior credential).\n- Deep expertise in MENA or Emerging Markets capital markets and portfolio risk construction.\n- Compelling executive presence with institutional allocators.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience managing Ucits or DIFC QIF/Exempt fund vehicles.\n- Arabic fluency.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $6,500–$10,000 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- DIFC-grade family medical coverage, life insurance, and annual flight ticket\n- 25 days paid annual leave plus performance-linked annual bonus\n- Full sponsorship for CFA, CAIA, or CQF study materials and exam fees\n- Modern DIFC office with Bloomberg terminals and research library\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Banking","seniority":"lead","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Portfolio Management","Asset Allocation","Risk Management","Financial Modeling","Client Management"],"reqs":["10+ years in institutional public-equity investment management with verifiable track record.","CFA Charterholder (mandatory or equivalent senior credential).","Deep expertise in MENA or Emerging Markets capital markets and portfolio risk construction.","Compelling executive presence with institutional allocators."],"lo":6500,"hi":10000,"days":2,"hours":15},{"company":"Gulfstream Capital","title":"Quantitative Analyst","description":"Gulfstream Capital is a DIFC-regulated asset management firm overseeing $3.8B across MENA public equities, sovereign/corporate fixed income, and quantitative multi-asset strategies for institutional and family-office clients. We're hiring a Quantitative Analyst to join the team (hybrid, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nResearch systematic equity factor signals, multi-asset risk covariance models, and transaction-cost analytics supporting Gulfstream's systematic and fundamental desks.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Research, backtest, and validate cross-sectional alpha signals and macro regime indicators in Python.\n- Build covariance, factor-attribution, and portfolio-optimization pipelines using clean SQL/Snowflake data.\n- Analyze execution slippage and market-impact costs to improve algorithmic order routing.\n- Guard rigorously against look-ahead bias, survivorship bias, and overfitting in research notebooks.\n- Partner with Data Engineering to productionize live daily risk and signal dashboards.\n\nRequirements:\n- Master's or PhD in a quantitative field (Financial Engineering, Statistics, Physics, CS, or Mathematics).\n- 3+ years of quantitative research or systematic risk modeling in asset management or prop trading.\n- Strong Python (numpy, pandas, scipy, cvxpy) and SQL skills.\n- Deep statistical rigor in time-series analysis and convex optimization.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience with Barra/Axioma factor risk models.\n- Familiarity with emerging-market liquidity constraints.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $3,300–$5,000 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- DIFC-grade family medical coverage, life insurance, and annual flight ticket\n- 25 days paid annual leave plus performance-linked annual bonus\n- Full sponsorship for CFA, CAIA, or CQF study materials and exam fees\n- Modern DIFC office with Bloomberg terminals and research library\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Banking","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Python","Statistics","Financial Modeling","Time Series","SQL"],"reqs":["Master's or PhD in a quantitative field (Financial Engineering, Statistics, Physics, CS, or Mathematics).","3+ years of quantitative research or systematic risk modeling in asset management or prop trading.","Strong Python (numpy, pandas, scipy, cvxpy) and SQL skills.","Deep statistical rigor in time-series analysis and convex optimization."],"lo":3300,"hi":5000,"days":9,"hours":20},{"company":"Gulfstream Capital","title":"Legal Counsel","description":"Gulfstream Capital is a DIFC-regulated asset management firm overseeing $3.8B across MENA public equities, sovereign/corporate fixed income, and quantitative multi-asset strategies for institutional and family-office clients. We're hiring a Legal Counsel to join the team (on-site, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nServe as in-house Legal Counsel in DIFC—advising Gulfstream's funds, investment teams, and Compliance Officer on fund structuring, DFSA rules, ISDAs, and IMAs.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Draft, review, and negotiate Investment Management Agreements (IMAs), side letters, subscription docs, and NDAs.\n- Advise on DIFC/DFSA fund structuring, cross-border marketing rules, and distribution partnerships.\n- Negotiate ISDA Master Agreements, prime brokerage, and custody contracts with global counterparties.\n- Support regulatory filings, board governance minutes, and vendor SaaS/data-license reviews.\n- Manage specialist external counsel across Cayman, Luxembourg, and GCC jurisdictions.\n\nRequirements:\n- Qualified lawyer (UK/US/Commonwealth or equivalent) with 6+ years PQE in funds, asset management, or financial services.\n- Strong experience with private/public fund formation, IMAs, and financial regulatory frameworks (DFSA/FCA/SEC).\n- Sharp commercial negotiation skills and ability to give clear, risk-calibrated advice to deal teams.\n\nNice to have:\n- Prior in-house DIFC / ADGM asset-management experience.\n- Familiarity with Shariah-compliant fund documentation.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $3,300–$5,000 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- DIFC-grade family medical coverage, life insurance, and annual flight ticket\n- 25 days paid annual leave plus performance-linked annual bonus\n- Full sponsorship for CFA, CAIA, or CQF study materials and exam fees\n- Modern DIFC office with Bloomberg terminals and research library\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Legal","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Corporate Law","Regulatory Compliance","Contracts","Financial Regulation","Negotiation"],"reqs":["Qualified lawyer (UK/US/Commonwealth or equivalent) with 6+ years PQE in funds, asset management, or financial services.","Strong experience with private/public fund formation, IMAs, and financial regulatory frameworks (DFSA/FCA/SEC).","Sharp commercial negotiation skills and ability to give clear, risk-calibrated advice to deal teams."],"lo":3300,"hi":5000,"days":16,"hours":1},{"company":"Harbor Finance","title":"Financial Controller","description":"Harbor Finance provides fractional CFO advisory, statutory audit, tax structuring, and cross-border accounting for high-growth SMEs in the UK and Europe. Our advisory squads combine chartered accountants with modern cloud finance tooling. We're hiring a Financial Controller to join the team (hybrid, London, UK).\n\nAbout the role:\nLead Harbor's 6-person London accounting delivery team—owning month-end close quality, statutory IFRS/UK GAAP reporting, and internal financial controls for key clients.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Own timely, audit-ready monthly, quarterly, and annual financial closes across key Harbor client accounts.\n- Lead, mentor, and review the work of 6 senior and junior accountants.\n- Design and strengthen internal financial controls, approval matrices, and revenue-recognition policies (IFRS 15/16).\n- Manage annual external audit processes cleanly from planning through signed statutory accounts.\n- Partner with Harbor CFOs on cash-flow governance, debt covenant reporting, and ERP upgrades.\n\nRequirements:\n- Qualified CPA, ACA, or ACCA with 8+ years of progressive accounting and controller experience.\n- Deep technical command of IFRS / UK GAAP, multi-entity consolidations, and internal controls.\n- 2+ years directly managing and developing an accounting team.\n- Calm, organized leadership during tight month-end and audit windows.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience scaling finance operations from Xero to NetSuite.\n- Multi-currency SaaS or marketplace accounting background.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $4,500–$6,800 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- Full study support and paid exam leave for ACCA, ACA, or CPA\n- 25 days paid holiday plus UK bank holidays and hybrid travel card\n- Private medical and dental cover plus pension matching\n- Flexible hybrid schedule (2–3 days/week in our London Bridge office)\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Finance","seniority":"lead","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"London, UK","skills":["Financial Reporting","IFRS","Team Leadership","Budgeting","Internal Controls"],"reqs":["Qualified CPA, ACA, or ACCA with 8+ years of progressive accounting and controller experience.","Deep technical command of IFRS / UK GAAP, multi-entity consolidations, and internal controls.","2+ years directly managing and developing an accounting team.","Calm, organized leadership during tight month-end and audit windows."],"lo":4500,"hi":6800,"days":2,"hours":6},{"company":"Horizon Policy Institute","title":"Economist","description":"Horizon Policy Institute is an independent economic and public-policy research institute in Geneva studying international trade, labor markets, climate transitions, and emerging-market fiscal resilience. Our economists publish peer-reviewed papers and advise multilateral agencies and ministries. We're hiring an Economist to join the team (hybrid, Geneva, Switzerland).\n\nAbout the role:\nDesign and execute empirical studies on labor-market transitions, trade barriers, and youth employment across Europe and MENA from our Geneva institute.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Formulate econometric identification strategies (DiD, IV, panel regressions) using household and administrative microdata.\n- Clean, link, and analyze large survey datasets in Stata and R with fully reproducible scripts.\n- Co-author working papers, peer-reviewed journal submissions, and clear 6-page policy briefs.\n- Present empirical findings to multilateral donors, labor ministries, and academic seminars.\n- Supervise Research Assistants on data preparation and robustness checks.\n\nRequirements:\n- Master's degree (or PhD) in Economics, Development Economics, or Public Policy.\n- 3+ years of applied empirical research experience with published working papers or policy reports.\n- Advanced econometric proficiency in Stata and/or R.\n- Clear academic and policy writing in English.\n\nNice to have:\n- French or Arabic proficiency for field partner coordination.\n- Experience evaluating active labor-market or trade-facilitation programs.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- 25 days paid vacation plus Swiss public holidays and hybrid/remote flexibility\n- Generous pension contributions and international health insurance allowance\n- Dedicated research travel, conference, and journal open-access budget\n- Sabbatical eligibility after 5 years of continuous research service\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Economics","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Geneva, Switzerland","skills":["Economics","Econometrics","Stata","Research","Policy Analysis"],"reqs":["Master's degree (or PhD) in Economics, Development Economics, or Public Policy.","3+ years of applied empirical research experience with published working papers or policy reports.","Advanced econometric proficiency in Stata and/or R.","Clear academic and policy writing in English."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":9,"hours":11},{"company":"Horizon Policy Institute","title":"Senior Economist (Macroeconomics)","description":"Horizon Policy Institute is an independent economic and public-policy research institute in Geneva studying international trade, labor markets, climate transitions, and emerging-market fiscal resilience. Our economists publish peer-reviewed papers and advise multilateral agencies and ministries. We're hiring a Senior Economist (Macroeconomics) to join the team (hybrid, Geneva, Switzerland).\n\nAbout the role:\nLead Horizon's flagship Macroeconomic & Fiscal Resilience program in Geneva—directing multi-country debt sustainability, inflation, and trade modeling.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Direct the institute's semi-annual macroeconomic outlook and fiscal-sustainability research agenda.\n- Build and maintain structural macro-econometric and DSGE/SVAR forecasting models in Python and Stata.\n- Lead senior advisory briefings for central bank officials, finance ministries, and multilateral partners.\n- Secure and steward multi-year research grants while mentoring 3 mid-level economists and RAs.\n- Represent Horizon at international policy forums and media briefings.\n\nRequirements:\n- PhD in Macroeconomics or International Economics (or Master's with 6+ years senior policy-institution experience).\n- Strong publication record in peer-reviewed journals or flagship multilateral reports.\n- Expertise in macro-econometric forecasting (Python/R/Stata) and fiscal/monetary policy analysis.\n- Compelling executive briefing and grant-leadership track record.\n\nNice to have:\n- Prior experience at an IMF/World Bank/OECD/Central Bank research division.\n- French fluency.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $3,300–$5,000 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- 25 days paid vacation plus Swiss public holidays and hybrid/remote flexibility\n- Generous pension contributions and international health insurance allowance\n- Dedicated research travel, conference, and journal open-access budget\n- Sabbatical eligibility after 5 years of continuous research service\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Economics","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Geneva, Switzerland","skills":["Macroeconomics","Econometrics","Forecasting","Python","Policy Writing"],"reqs":["PhD in Macroeconomics or International Economics (or Master's with 6+ years senior policy-institution experience).","Strong publication record in peer-reviewed journals or flagship multilateral reports.","Expertise in macro-econometric forecasting (Python/R/Stata) and fiscal/monetary policy analysis.","Compelling executive briefing and grant-leadership track record."],"lo":3300,"hi":5000,"days":16,"hours":16},{"company":"Horizon Policy Institute","title":"Research Assistant (Economics)","description":"Horizon Policy Institute is an independent economic and public-policy research institute in Geneva studying international trade, labor markets, climate transitions, and emerging-market fiscal resilience. Our economists publish peer-reviewed papers and advise multilateral agencies and ministries. We're hiring a Research Assistant (Economics) to join the team (hybrid, Geneva, Switzerland).\n\nAbout the role:\nSupport Horizon's Geneva economists with empirical data cleaning, reproducible statistical tables, literature reviews, and policy-report graphics.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Clean, merge, and document large microeconomic and trade datasets in R, Stata, and Excel.\n- Run descriptive statistics, regression replication scripts, and sensitivity checks under economist guidance.\n- Produce publication-grade charts, LaTeX/Word regression tables, and clear data appendices.\n- Conduct structured literature searches and verify citations for working papers.\n- Coordinate with partner statistical agencies on data-access requests.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's (or Master's) degree in Economics, Statistics, or Quantitative Social Sciences.\n- Hands-on coursework or project proficiency in R or Stata plus strong Excel skills.\n- Meticulous data-hygiene habits and enthusiasm for reproducible empirical research.\n- Strong written English.\n\nNice to have:\n- Knowledge of LaTeX, Git, or Python.\n- Interest in pursuing a PhD or policy career after 2 years.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,100–$1,800 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- 25 days paid vacation plus Swiss public holidays and hybrid/remote flexibility\n- Generous pension contributions and international health 