ional context to mixed-methods research projects.\n\nRequirements:\n- 2+ years in a think tank, public-policy consultancy, multilateral agency, or government advisory unit.\n- Master's degree in Public Policy, International Economics, or Political Economy.\n- Exceptional, jargon-free policy writing portfolio in English.\n- Strong data-literacy and comfort working independently in a remote setup.\n\nNice to have:\n- Working fluency in French, Arabic, or German.\n- Experience with Datawrapper or interactive policy dashboards.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Remote)\n- 25 days paid vacation plus Swiss public holidays and hybrid/remote flexibility\n- Generous pension contributions and international health insurance allowance\n- Dedicated research travel, conference, and journal open-access budget\n- Sabbatical eligibility after 5 years of continuous research service\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Economics","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"remote","location":"Remote","skills":["Policy Analysis","Research","Writing","Economics","Data Visualization"],"reqs":["2+ years in a think tank, public-policy consultancy, multilateral agency, or government advisory unit.","Master's degree in Public Policy, International Economics, or Political Economy.","Exceptional, jargon-free policy writing portfolio in English.","Strong data-literacy and comfort working independently in a remote setup."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":9,"hours":2},{"company":"Horizon Policy Institute","title":"Development Economics Intern","description":"Horizon Policy Institute is an independent economic and public-policy research institute in Geneva studying international trade, labor markets, climate transitions, and emerging-market fiscal resilience. Our economists publish peer-reviewed papers and advise multilateral agencies and ministries. We're hiring a Development Economics Intern to join the team (remote).\n\nAbout the role:\nA 12-week remote research internship assisting Horizon's labor and development economists with literature synthesis, survey checks, and policy note drafting.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Assist economists with systematic literature reviews on labor formalization and SME productivity.\n- Help clean and verify country-level macro/survey spreadsheets and check chart accuracy.\n- Draft concise 1-page research summaries and blog highlights for Horizon's newsletter.\n- Join weekly virtual research seminars and receive structured career mentoring.\n\nRequirements:\n- Currently enrolled in (or recently graduated from) an Economics, Development Studies, or Public Policy program.\n- Strong analytical writing in English and solid Excel skills.\n- Genuine curiosity about empirical development economics.\n\nNice to have:\n- Exposure to Stata, R, or Python.\n- Knowledge of MENA or Sub-Saharan African economic context.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $450–$800 USD / month (Internship, Remote)\n- 25 days paid vacation plus Swiss public holidays and hybrid/remote flexibility\n- Generous pension contributions and international health insurance allowance\n- Dedicated research travel, conference, and journal open-access budget\n- Sabbatical eligibility after 5 years of continuous research service\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Application & portfolio/CV review (2–3 business days)\n- 2. 30-minute conversation with your team mentor — focused on projects and curiosity, no trick questions\n- 3. Final placement confirmation and start-date onboarding","field":"Economics","seniority":"intern","type":"internship","mode":"remote","location":"Remote","skills":["Economics","Research","Excel","Writing"],"reqs":["Currently enrolled in (or recently graduated from) an Economics, Development Studies, or Public Policy program.","Strong analytical writing in English and solid Excel skills.","Genuine curiosity about empirical development economics."],"lo":450,"hi":800,"days":16,"hours":7},{"company":"Helix Biolabs","title":"Research Scientist (Molecular Biology)","description":"Helix Biolabs develops molecular diagnostic assays, NGS sequencing panels, and automated laboratory instruments for inherited and rare genetic conditions. Operating CLIA-certified and GMP-compliant facilities in Cambridge/Boston, we bridge bench science with clinical care. We're hiring a Research Scientist (Molecular Biology) to join the team (on-site, Boston, USA).\n\nAbout the role:\nLead assay R&D in Cambridge/Boston—developing sensitive multiplex qPCR, CRISPR-based detection, and NGS library-prep workflows for rare genetic diagnostics.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Design and execute wet-lab feasibility and analytical validation experiments (LoD, specificity, precision).\n- Develop novel nucleic-acid extraction, multiplex PCR, and CRISPR-Cas diagnostic assays.\n- Analyze experimental results rigorously using R/Python or GraphPad Prism and present at R&D reviews.\n- Mentor 2–3 Research Associates on assay troubleshooting, ELN documentation, and GLP habits.\n- Partner with Systems Engineering and Regulatory teams to transfer validated assays into manufacturing.\n\nRequirements:\n- PhD in Molecular Biology, Genetics, Biochemistry, or Bioengineering (or MS with 6+ years industry R&D).\n- Deep hands-on expertise in qPCR/ddPCR, NGS library preparation, CRISPR systems, and cell culture.\n- Track record taking diagnostic or molecular assays from bench concept to analytical validation.\n- Strong experimental design (DoE), statistical analysis, and team mentoring skills.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience under FDA IVD / CLIA / ISO 13485 design-control frameworks.\n- Familiarity with automated liquid handlers (Hamilton/Tecan).\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $3,300–$5,000 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive US medical, dental, and vision insurance (90% employer-paid)\n- 401(k) with 5% company match, equity grants, and 20 days PTO\n- On-site commuter transit subsidy and fully stocked lab-break kitchens\n- Annual $2,000 scientific conference and continuing education stipend\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Science","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Boston, USA","skills":["Molecular Biology","PCR","CRISPR","Cell Culture","Data Analysis"],"reqs":["PhD in Molecular Biology, Genetics, Biochemistry, or Bioengineering (or MS with 6+ years industry R&D).","Deep hands-on expertise in qPCR/ddPCR, NGS library preparation, CRISPR systems, and cell culture.","Track record taking diagnostic or molecular assays from bench concept to analytical validation.","Strong experimental design (DoE), statistical analysis, and team mentoring skills."],"lo":3300,"hi":5000,"days":2,"hours":12},{"company":"Helix Biolabs","title":"Laboratory Technician","description":"Helix Biolabs develops molecular diagnostic assays, NGS sequencing panels, and automated laboratory instruments for inherited and rare genetic conditions. Operating CLIA-certified and GMP-compliant facilities in Cambridge/Boston, we bridge bench science with clinical care. We're hiring a Laboratory Technician to join the team (on-site, Boston, USA).\n\nAbout the role:\nSupport Helix's Boston molecular testing lab—receiving clinical specimens, preparing nucleic-acid extractions, running high-throughput assays, and maintaining spotless ELN logs.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Accession incoming biological samples, verify chain-of-custody barcodes, and store specimens properly.\n- Prepare buffers/reagents and execute DNA/RNA extraction and PCR setup with precision pipetting.\n- Operate automated liquid handlers and plate readers following written SOPs.\n- Perform daily lab housekeeping, biosafety cabinet checks, and biohazard waste protocols.\n- Document every run accurately in electronic lab notebooks (ELN) and LIMS.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's or Associate degree in Biology, Chemistry, Biotechnology, or Clinical Lab Science.\n- Hands-on academic or industry wet-lab experience with micropipetting, aseptic technique, and PCR basics.\n- Meticulous attention to SOP compliance, sample labeling, and lab safety.\n- Reliable team player comfortable working on-site in our Boston laboratory.\n\nNice to have:\n- 6+ months experience in a CLIA, GLP, or biotech screening lab.\n- Familiarity with LIMS barcode workflows.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,100–$1,800 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive US medical, dental, and vision insurance (90% employer-paid)\n- 401(k) with 5% company match, equity grants, and 20 days PTO\n- On-site commuter transit subsidy and fully stocked lab-break kitchens\n- Annual $2,000 scientific conference and continuing education stipend\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Science","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Boston, USA","skills":["Laboratory Testing","Sample Handling","Lab Safety","Documentation","Pipetting"],"reqs":["Bachelor's or Associate degree in Biology, Chemistry, Biotechnology, or Clinical Lab Science.","Hands-on academic or industry wet-lab experience with micropipetting, aseptic technique, and PCR basics.","Meticulous attention to SOP compliance, sample labeling, and lab safety.","Reliable team player comfortable working on-site in our Boston laboratory."],"lo":1100,"hi":1800,"days":9,"hours":17},{"company":"Helix Biolabs","title":"Bioinformatics Scientist","description":"Helix Biolabs develops molecular diagnostic assays, NGS sequencing panels, and automated laboratory instruments for inherited and rare genetic conditions. Operating CLIA-certified and GMP-compliant facilities in Cambridge/Boston, we bridge bench science with clinical care. We're hiring a Bioinformatics Scientist to join the team (hybrid, Boston, USA).\n\nAbout the role:\nBuild reproducible NGS variant-calling pipelines and statistical QC tools supporting Helix's inherited-disease panels from Boston.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Develop and maintain Nextflow/Snakemake bioinformatics pipelines for targeted and whole-exome NGS data.\n- Implement variant-calling, CNV detection, and annotation workflows with clear sensitivity/specificity benchmarks.\n- Analyze assay R&D sequencing runs in Python and R to diagnose probe bias, coverage drops, or contamination.\n- Build interactive QC summary reports for wet-lab scientists and clinical directors.\n- Maintain version-controlled, containerised workflows (Docker/Singularity) ready for clinical validation.\n\nRequirements:\n- Master's or PhD in Bioinformatics, Computational Biology, or Genomics (or BS with 4+ years NGS experience).\n- Strong Python and R programming skills alongside Linux CLI and Git.\n- Hands-on experience with standard NGS tools (BWA, GATK, Samtools, bcftools) and variant interpretation.\n- Solid statistical grounding in genomics QC and assay validation.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience with Nextflow/WDL on AWS Batch and Docker.\n- Familiarity with ACMG variant classification guidelines.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- Comprehensive US medical, dental, and vision insurance (90% employer-paid)\n- 401(k) with 5% company match, equity grants, and 20 days PTO\n- On-site commuter transit subsidy and fully stocked lab-break kitchens\n- Annual $2,000 scientific conference and continuing education stipend\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Science","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Boston, USA","skills":["Python","R","Genomics","Bioinformatics","Statistics"],"reqs":["Master's or PhD in Bioinformatics, Computational Biology, or Genomics (or BS with 4+ years NGS experience).","Strong Python and R programming skills alongside Linux CLI and Git.","Hands-on experience with standard NGS tools (BWA, GATK, Samtools, bcftools) and variant interpretation.","Solid statistical grounding in genomics QC and assay validation."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":16,"hours":22},{"company":"Helix Biolabs","title":"Quality Control Chemist","description":"Helix Biolabs develops molecular diagnostic assays, NGS sequencing panels, and automated laboratory instruments for inherited and rare genetic conditions. Operating CLIA-certified and GMP-compliant facilities in Cambridge/Boston, we bridge bench science with clinical care. We're hiring a Quality Control Chemist to join the team (on-site, Boston, USA).\n\nAbout the role:\nEnsure every oligonucleotide probe, reagent kit, and diagnostic lot manufactured at Helix's Boston facility passes strict GMP analytical release specifications.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Perform analytical release testing on raw materials, intermediates, and finished reagent kits via HPLC, UV-Vis, and Karl Fischer.\n- Execute stability pull-point testing and prepare clear Certificates of Analysis (CoAs).\n- Investigate Out-of-Specification (OOS) / Out-of-Trend (OOT) results and support CAPA root-cause reviews.\n- Author and revise QC test methods and SOPs in accordance with 21 CFR Part 820 / ISO 13485.\n- Maintain instrument calibration logs and audit-ready GMP documentation.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's degree in Chemistry, Biochemistry, or Analytical Sciences.\n- 2+ years of Quality Control experience inside a GMP / ISO 13485 biotech or pharma laboratory.\n- Hands-on proficiency with HPLC/UPLC (Empower or Chromeleon), UV spectrophotometry, and wet-chemistry methods.\n- Rigorous ALCOA+ GDP (Good Documentation Practices) habits.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience testing oligonucleotides, enzymes, or diagnostic IVD reagents.\n- Experience participating in FDA or ISO regulatory audits.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive US medical, dental, and vision insurance (90% employer-paid)\n- 401(k) with 5% company match, equity grants, and 20 days PTO\n- On-site commuter transit subsidy and fully stocked lab-break kitchens\n- Annual $2,000 scientific conference and continuing education stipend\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Science","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Boston, USA","skills":["Analytical Chemistry","HPLC","GMP","Quality Control","Documentation"],"reqs":["Bachelor's degree in Chemistry, Biochemistry, or Analytical Sciences.","2+ years of Quality Control experience inside a GMP / ISO 13485 biotech or pharma laboratory.","Hands-on proficiency with HPLC/UPLC (Empower or Chromeleon), UV spectrophotometry, and wet-chemistry methods.","Rigorous ALCOA+ GDP (Good Documentation Practices) habits."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":2,"hours":3},{"company":"Helix Biolabs","title":"Clinical Research Associate","description":"Helix Biolabs develops molecular diagnostic assays, NGS sequencing panels, and automated laboratory instruments for inherited and rare genetic conditions. Operating CLIA-certified and GMP-compliant facilities in Cambridge/Boston, we bridge bench science with clinical care. We're hiring a Clinical Research Associate to join the team (hybrid, Boston, USA).\n\nAbout the role:\nMonitor multi-center clinical validation studies across US hospital sites for Helix's next-generation diagnostic panels—ensuring ICH-GCP integrity and clean trial data.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Conduct site qualification, initiation, interim monitoring, and close-out visits (remote and on-site).\n- Perform Source Document Verification (SDV), check informed consent compliance, and verify IRB approvals.\n- Track specimen shipment logs, EDC query resolution, and protocol deviations across 8–12 clinical sites.\n- Maintain up-to-date Trial Master File (eTMF) documentation in inspection-ready condition.\n- Build collaborative, supportive relationships with Principal Investigators and site study coordinators.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's degree in Life Sciences, Nursing, or Health Sciences.\n- 2+ years as a Clinical Research Associate (CRA) monitoring clinical or diagnostic device studies.\n- Strong command of ICH-GCP, FDA regulations, EDC systems (Medidata Rave/REDCap), and eTMF.\n- Willingness to travel regionally (~25–35%) to US clinical sites.\n\nNice to have:\n- ACRP or SOCRA certification.\n- Prior experience monitoring IVD / diagnostic biomarker validation trials.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- Comprehensive US medical, dental, and vision insurance (90% employer-paid)\n- 401(k) with 5% company match, equity grants, and 20 days PTO\n- On-site commuter transit subsidy and fully stocked lab-break kitchens\n- Annual $2,000 scientific conference and continuing education stipend\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Science","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Boston, USA","skills":["Clinical Trials","GCP","Data Management","Regulatory Compliance","Communication"],"reqs":["Bachelor's degree in Life Sciences, Nursing, or Health Sciences.","2+ years as a Clinical Research Associate (CRA) monitoring clinical or diagnostic device studies.","Strong command of ICH-GCP, FDA regulations, EDC systems (Medidata Rave/REDCap), and eTMF.","Willingness to travel regionally (~25–35%) to US clinical sites."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":9,"hours":8},{"company":"Helix Biolabs","title":"Physicist (R&D Imaging)","description":"Helix Biolabs develops molecular diagnostic assays, NGS sequencing panels, and automated laboratory instruments for inherited and rare genetic conditions. Operating CLIA-certified and GMP-compliant facilities in Cambridge/Boston, we bridge bench science with clinical care. We're hiring a Physicist (R&D Imaging) to join the team (on-site, Boston, USA).\n\nAbout the role:\nArchitect fluorescence optical detection and high-speed image-processing subsystems for Helix's next-generation automated molecular diagnostic analyzers in Boston.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Design multi-channel fluorescence optical trains (LED/laser illumination, dichroics, CMOS sensors) in Zemax/OpticStudio.\n- Model signal-to-noise budgets, stray light, and thermal drift across compact benchtop instrument prototypes.\n- Develop image registration, spot-calling, and signal-processing algorithms in MATLAB and Python.\n- Align, characterize, and test optical breadboards alongside mechanical and firmware engineers.\n- Author tolerance specifications for optical component suppliers and manufacturing transfer.\n\nRequirements:\n- PhD in Physics, Applied Optics, or Biomedical Engineering (or MS with 5+ years instrument R&D).\n- Strong hands-on experience designing fluorescence microscopy or optical diagnostic hardware.\n- Proficiency in Zemax/Code V, MATLAB/Python image & signal processing, and optical bench alignment.\n- Collaborative track record shipping multidisciplinary hardware prototypes.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience with sequencing flow-cell imaging or microfluidic chip optics.\n- Familiarity with Design for Manufacturing (DFM) of optical assemblies.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $3,300–$5,000 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive US medical, dental, and vision insurance (90% employer-paid)\n- 401(k) with 5% company match, equity grants, and 20 days PTO\n- On-site commuter transit subsidy and fully stocked lab-break kitchens\n- Annual $2,000 scientific conference and continuing education stipend\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Science","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Boston, USA","skills":["Physics","Optics","MATLAB","Signal Processing","Research"],"reqs":["PhD in Physics, Applied Optics, or Biomedical Engineering (or MS with 5+ years instrument R&D).","Strong hands-on experience designing fluorescence microscopy or optical diagnostic hardware.","Proficiency in Zemax/Code V, MATLAB/Python image & signal processing, and optical bench alignment.","Collaborative track record shipping multidisciplinary hardware prototypes."],"lo":3300,"hi":5000,"days":16,"hours":13},{"company":"Terra Labs","title":"Environmental Scientist","description":"Terra Labs provides accredited environmental monitoring—sampling air quality, municipal water, industrial soils, and food-chain microbiology for European cities and manufacturers. Our Amsterdam scientists pair field testing with predictive GIS and pollution-forecasting models. We're hiring an Environmental Scientist to join the team (hybrid, Amsterdam, Netherlands).\n\nAbout the role:\nLead air-quality, groundwater, and urban soil monitoring campaigns across Dutch municipalities—turning field measurements into spatial GIS risk assessments.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Plan and conduct accredited field sampling campaigns for air particulates, surface/groundwater, and soil.\n- Operate and calibrate portable gas analyzers, multiparameter water probes, and particulate monitors.\n- Map spatial contamination plumes and sensor networks using QGIS / ArcGIS.\n- Analyze laboratory results against EU/Dutch environmental thresholds and draft clear client assessment reports.\n- Coordinate cleanly with municipal planners, industrial HSE teams, and Terra's Amsterdam lab.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's or Master's degree in Environmental Science, Earth Sciences, or Ecology.\n- 2+ years of environmental field sampling and technical assessment experience.\n- Working proficiency with QGIS or ArcGIS and environmental data analysis.\n- Clear technical report writing in English (Dutch is a strong advantage) and valid EU driving license.\n\nNice to have:\n- VCA safety certification or Dutch BRL sampling accreditation.\n- Experience with IoT air-quality sensor networks.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- 25 days paid annual leave, 8% Dutch holiday allowance, and NS Business transit card\n- Hybrid lab/remote flexibility and $1,000 home-office ergonomic stipend\n- Annual sustainability & field-safety training budget\n- Cycle-to-work lease plan and pension contribution\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Science","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Amsterdam, Netherlands","skills":["Environmental Science","Field Sampling","GIS","Data Analysis","Report Writing"],"reqs":["Bachelor's or Master's degree in Environmental Science, Earth Sciences, or Ecology.","2+ years of environmental field sampling and technical assessment experience.","Working proficiency with QGIS or ArcGIS and environmental data analysis.","Clear technical report writing in English (Dutch is a strong advantage) and valid EU driving license."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":2,"hours":18},{"company":"Terra Labs","title":"Data Scientist","description":"Terra Labs provides accredited environmental monitoring—sampling air quality, municipal water, industrial soils, and food-chain microbiology for European cities and manufacturers. Our Amsterdam scientists pair field testing with predictive GIS and pollution-forecasting models. We're hiring a Data Scientist to join the team (remote).\n\nAbout the role:\nBuild spatiotemporal models that forecast urban air-quality spikes, water-network anomalies, and industrial emissions for Terra Labs' European city clients.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Develop and validate spatiotemporal machine learning models fusing IoT sensor telemetry, weather, and traffic data.\n- Engineer clean feature pipelines in Python and SQL and deploy models reliably with engineering.\n- Diagnose sensor drift, missing-data bias, and seasonal shifts using rigorous statistical diagnostics.\n- Create clear visual explanations of model drivers and uncertainty intervals for municipal decision-makers.\n- Collaborate with environmental scientists to keep physical domain constraints front and center.\n\nRequirements:\n- 3+ years of applied data science experience shipping statistical or ML models into production.\n- Strong Python (scikit-learn, pandas, LightGBM/PyTorch) and SQL skills.\n- Solid statistical foundation in time-series, spatial modeling, and cross-validation.\n- Clear communication with non-technical domain experts.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience with geospatial Python (GeoPandas, Rasterio) or IoT environmental telemetry.\n- Master's in Data Science, Statistics, or Environmental Engineering.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Remote)\n- 25 days paid annual leave, 8% Dutch holiday allowance, and NS Business transit card\n- Hybrid lab/remote flexibility and $1,000 home-office ergonomic stipend\n- Annual sustainability & field-safety training budget\n- Cycle-to-work lease plan and pension contribution\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Science","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"remote","location":"Remote","skills":["Python","Machine Learning","SQL","Statistics","Data Visualization"],"reqs":["3+ years of applied data science experience shipping statistical or ML models into production.","Strong Python (scikit-learn, pandas, LightGBM/PyTorch) and SQL skills.","Solid statistical foundation in time-series, spatial modeling, and cross-validation.","Clear communication with non-technical domain experts."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":9,"hours":23},{"company":"Terra Labs","title":"Food Safety Specialist","description":"Terra Labs provides accredited environmental monitoring—sampling air quality, municipal water, industrial soils, and food-chain microbiology for European cities and manufacturers. Our Amsterdam scientists pair field testing with predictive GIS and pollution-forecasting models. We're hiring a Food Safety Specialist to join the team (on-site, Amsterdam, Netherlands).\n\nAbout the role:\nAudit European food manufacturers and cold-chain kitchens from Amsterdam—running microbiological hygiene verification and guiding clients on HACCP & BRCGS compliance.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Conduct on-site food safety, GMP hygiene, and HACCP compliance audits across food processing and catering facilities.\n- Collect surface swabs, water samples, and finished-product samples for microbiological testing.\n- Interpret pathogen/spoilage test results and help clients investigate root causes of non-conformities.\n- Design practical, clear HACCP plans, allergen controls, and sanitation SOPs tailored to each facility.\n- Deliver engaging food-hygiene training workshops for production floor staff.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's or Master's degree in Food Science, Food Technology, or Microbiology.\n- 2+ years in food-safety QA, HACCP management, or third-party food auditing.\n- Strong working knowledge of EU food-safety regulations, HACCP, and ISO 22000 / BRCGS.\n- Fluent English (Dutch or German helpful) and willingness to visit client plants across the Netherlands.\n\nNice to have:\n- Lead Auditor certification (ISO 22000 / FSSC 22000).\n- Hands-on food microbiology lab experience.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- 25 days paid annual leave, 8% Dutch holiday allowance, and NS Business transit card\n- Hybrid lab/remote flexibility and $1,000 home-office ergonomic stipend\n- Annual sustainability & field-safety training budget\n- Cycle-to-work lease plan and pension contribution\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Science","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Amsterdam, Netherlands","skills":["Food Safety","HACCP","Quality Control","Microbiology","Auditing"],"reqs":["Bachelor's or Master's degree in Food Science, Food Technology, or Microbiology.","2+ years in food-safety QA, HACCP management, or third-party food auditing.","Strong working knowledge of EU food-safety regulations, HACCP, and ISO 22000 / BRCGS.","Fluent English (Dutch or German helpful) and willingness to visit client plants across the Netherlands."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":16,"hours":4},{"company":"Terra Labs","title":"Research Intern (Climate)","description":"Terra Labs provides accredited environmental monitoring—sampling air quality, municipal water, industrial soils, and food-chain microbiology for European cities and manufacturers. Our Amsterdam scientists pair field testing with predictive GIS and pollution-forecasting models. We're hiring a Research Intern (Climate) to join the team (hybrid, Amsterdam, Netherlands).\n\nAbout the role:\nA 16-week paid internship in Amsterdam analyzing urban heat-island and air-quality datasets alongside Terra Labs' climate and data science team.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Clean and explore historical urban air-quality, temperature, and satellite-derived green-cover datasets in Python.\n- Generate clear summary plots and statistical comparisons across Dutch and European test neighborhoods.\n- Review peer-reviewed climate-adaptation literature to support municipal project proposals.\n- Present findings and code notebooks at a team-wide lunch-and-learn.\n\nRequirements:\n- Currently enrolled in a Bachelor's or Master's program in Environmental Science, Climate, Data Science, or Physics.\n- Working familiarity with Python (pandas/matplotlib) or R for data exploration.\n- Clear written English and curiosity about urban climate measurement.\n\nNice to have:\n- Coursework in GIS, remote sensing, or atmospheric chemistry.\n- Comfortable working hybrid in Amsterdam.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $450–$800 USD / month (Internship, Hybrid)\n- 25 days paid annual leave, 8% Dutch holiday allowance, and NS Business transit card\n- Hybrid lab/remote flexibility and $1,000 home-office ergonomic stipend\n- Annual sustainability & field-safety training budget\n- Cycle-to-work lease plan and pension contribution\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Application & portfolio/CV review (2–3 business days)\n- 2. 30-minute conversation with your team mentor — focused on projects and curiosity, no trick questions\n- 3. Final placement confirmation and start-date onboarding","field":"Science","seniority":"intern","type":"internship","mode":"hybrid","location":"Amsterdam, Netherlands","skil