benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive UAE family medical insurance and annual airfare allowance\n- 25 days paid annual leave plus site-rotation / offshore uplift where applicable\n- Transport and site-mobilization allowance plus full PPE gear\n- Paid sponsorship for NEBOSH, TUV Functional Safety, and Chartered Engineer status\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Engineering","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Abu Dhabi, UAE","skills":["Process Engineering","Aspen HYSYS","P&ID","HAZOP","Process Safety"],"reqs":["Bachelor's degree in Chemical Engineering.","3+ years of process design or plant operations engineering in oil & gas, petrochemicals, or water/energy.","Strong hands-on proficiency in Aspen HYSYS, P&ID development, and API/ASME process standards.","Practical experience participating in HAZOP reviews."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":9,"hours":14},{"company":"Delta Process Engineering","title":"Petroleum Engineer","description":"Delta Process Engineering delivers EPC process design, safety engineering, instrumentation, and plant optimization for energy, petrochemicals, and industrial utilities across Abu Dhabi and the wider GCC. Our multidisciplinary engineers support brownfield revamps and greenfield modular skids. We're hiring a Petroleum Engineer to join the team (on-site, Abu Dhabi, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nLead reservoir surveillance, production-optimization studies, and well-intervention programs for upstream client assets out of Abu Dhabi.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Build and update reservoir simulation and nodal-analysis models to forecast field recovery and well deliverability.\n- Design well-stimulation, artificial-lift, and water-shutoff intervention programs to boost mature field output.\n- Analyze well-test pressure transients (PTA), production logs (PLT), and decline curves.\n- Review drilling/completion proposals for reservoir compatibility and integrity.\n- Present technical field-development recommendations to client asset managers.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's or Master's degree in Petroleum Engineering.\n- 6+ years of upstream reservoir or production engineering experience.\n- Strong command of Petrel / Eclipse / Prosper / GAP / Saphir.\n- Track record delivering safe, cost-effective production optimization gains.\n\nNice to have:\n- GCC carbonate reservoir or EOR (CO2/polymer) experience.\n- SPE active member with technical publications.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $3,300–$5,000 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive UAE family medical insurance and annual airfare allowance\n- 25 days paid annual leave plus site-rotation / offshore uplift where applicable\n- Transport and site-mobilization allowance plus full PPE gear\n- Paid sponsorship for NEBOSH, TUV Functional Safety, and Chartered Engineer status\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Engineering","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Abu Dhabi, UAE","skills":["Petroleum Engineering","Reservoir Engineering","Drilling","Production Optimization","Petrel"],"reqs":["Bachelor's or Master's degree in Petroleum Engineering.","6+ years of upstream reservoir or production engineering experience.","Strong command of Petrel / Eclipse / Prosper / GAP / Saphir.","Track record delivering safe, cost-effective production optimization gains."],"lo":3300,"hi":5000,"days":16,"hours":19},{"company":"Delta Process Engineering","title":"HSE Officer","description":"Delta Process Engineering delivers EPC process design, safety engineering, instrumentation, and plant optimization for energy, petrochemicals, and industrial utilities across Abu Dhabi and the wider GCC. Our multidisciplinary engineers support brownfield revamps and greenfield modular skids. We're hiring a HSE Officer to join the team (on-site, Abu Dhabi, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nProtect frontline engineering and contractor crews across industrial plant sites in Abu Dhabi by driving proactive Permit-to-Work controls, risk assessments, and safety culture.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Conduct daily site safety walkdowns, confined-space/hot-work Permit-to-Work audits, and gas-testing checks.\n- Deliver engaging morning toolbox talks and site safety inductions for multidisciplinary crews.\n- Review Job Safety Analyses (JSAs) and lifting plans ahead of high-risk maintenance activities.\n- Lead root-cause incident and near-miss investigations and track corrective actions to closure.\n- Maintain ISO 45001 HSE statistics, emergency drill logs, and client audit readiness.\n\nRequirements:\n- NEBOSH International General Certificate (IGC) or Diploma (or OSHA 30 + degree).\n- 3+ years of industrial HSE officer experience in oil & gas, process plants, or heavy construction.\n- Strong working knowledge of PTW systems, LOTO, working at heights, and ISO 45001.\n- Firm yet respectful communication style across multicultural site crews.\n\nNice to have:\n- ADNOC / OSHAD practitioner registration.\n- First Aid / Fire Warden instructor qualification.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive UAE family medical insurance and annual airfare allowance\n- 25 days paid annual leave plus site-rotation / offshore uplift where applicable\n- Transport and site-mobilization allowance plus full PPE gear\n- Paid sponsorship for NEBOSH, TUV Functional Safety, and Chartered Engineer status\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Engineering","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Abu Dhabi, UAE","skills":["Health & Safety","Risk Assessment","NEBOSH","Incident Investigation","ISO 45001"],"reqs":["NEBOSH International General Certificate (IGC) or Diploma (or OSHA 30 + degree).","3+ years of industrial HSE officer experience in oil & gas, process plants, or heavy construction.","Strong working knowledge of PTW systems, LOTO, working at heights, and ISO 45001.","Firm yet respectful communication style across multicultural site crews."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":2,"hours":0},{"company":"Delta Process Engineering","title":"Instrumentation & Control Engineer","description":"Delta Process Engineering delivers EPC process design, safety engineering, instrumentation, and plant optimization for energy, petrochemicals, and industrial utilities across Abu Dhabi and the wider GCC. Our multidisciplinary engineers support brownfield revamps and greenfield modular skids. We're hiring an Instrumentation & Control Engineer to join the team (on-site, Abu Dhabi, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nEngineer field instrumentation specs, PLC/DCS control logic, and SCADA HMI screens for automated process skids and plant upgrades in Abu Dhabi.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Prepare instrument index, I/O lists, hook-up drawings, control-valve sizing, and loop diagrams in AutoCAD/SPI.\n- Develop and test PLC/SIS logic (Siemens, Allen-Bradley, or Triconex) and SCADA/HMI graphics.\n- Lead Factory Acceptance Tests (FAT) and Site Acceptance Tests (SAT) with clients and panel builders.\n- Support loop checking, transmitter calibration, and ESD cause-and-effect testing during commissioning.\n- Review vendor instrumentation packages for SIL compliance and hazardous-area (ATEX/IECEx) certification.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's degree in Electrical, Electronics, or Instrumentation & Control Engineering.\n- 3+ years designing and commissioning industrial I&C / PLC / SCADA systems.\n- Strong familiarity with P&ID control narratives, ISA datasheets, and IEC 61511 functional safety.\n- Comfort working both in the Abu Dhabi office and on industrial plant sites during SAT.\n\nNice to have:\n- TUV Functional Safety Engineer (SIS) certificate.\n- Experience with SmartPlant Instrumentation (SPI / INTools).\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive UAE family medical insurance and annual airfare allowance\n- 25 days paid annual leave plus site-rotation / offshore uplift where applicable\n- Transport and site-mobilization allowance plus full PPE gear\n- Paid sponsorship for NEBOSH, TUV Functional Safety, and Chartered Engineer status\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Engineering","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Abu Dhabi, UAE","skills":["Instrumentation","PLC","SCADA","Control Systems","AutoCAD"],"reqs":["Bachelor's degree in Electrical, Electronics, or Instrumentation & Control Engineering.","3+ years designing and commissioning industrial I&C / PLC / SCADA systems.","Strong familiarity with P&ID control narratives, ISA datasheets, and IEC 61511 functional safety.","Comfort working both in the Abu Dhabi office and on industrial plant sites during SAT."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":9,"hours":5},{"company":"Delta Process Engineering","title":"Industrial Engineer","description":"Delta Process Engineering delivers EPC process design, safety engineering, instrumentation, and plant optimization for energy, petrochemicals, and industrial utilities across Abu Dhabi and the wider GCC. Our multidisciplinary engineers support brownfield revamps and greenfield modular skids. We're hiring an Industrial Engineer to join the team (on-site, Abu Dhabi, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nOptimize plant throughput, maintenance turnaround scheduling, and modular fabrication workflows across Delta's industrial and energy client facilities in the UAE.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Map end-to-end production and maintenance workflows (VSM) to pinpoint bottlenecks, rework, and idle time.\n- Lead DMAIC / Kaizen continuous-improvement projects with plant supervisors and technicians.\n- Build discrete-event simulation and capacity models in Excel/Arena/Simio to justify layout or staffing changes.\n- Design clear visual SOPs, 5S standards, and daily tiered KPI boards on the shop floor.\n- Quantify realized cost, cycle-time, and scrap reductions cleanly for plant directors.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's degree in Industrial Engineering or Manufacturing Systems.\n- 2+ years applying Lean / Six Sigma in manufacturing, fabrication, or industrial operations.\n- Lean Six Sigma Green Belt (or Black Belt) certification.\n- Strong quantitative modeling skills and hands-on shop-floor credibility.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience in heavy fabrication, modular skid assembly, or chemical packaging.\n- Power BI or Minitab proficiency.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive UAE family medical insurance and annual airfare allowance\n- 25 days paid annual leave plus site-rotation / offshore uplift where applicable\n- Transport and site-mobilization allowance plus full PPE gear\n- Paid sponsorship for NEBOSH, TUV Functional Safety, and Chartered Engineer status\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Engineering","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Abu 