rks CSWA / CSWP certification.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,100–$1,800 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive UAE family medical insurance and annual airfare allowance\n- 25 days paid annual leave plus site-rotation / offshore uplift where applicable\n- Transport and site-mobilization allowance plus full PPE gear\n- Paid sponsorship for NEBOSH, TUV Functional Safety, and Chartered Engineer status\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Engineering","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Abu Dhabi, UAE","skills":["SolidWorks","Mechanical Design","AutoCAD","GD&T","Prototyping"],"reqs":["Bachelor's degree in Mechanical Engineering.","1+ year of mechanical CAD design experience (including substantial university/capstone or internship work).","Strong proficiency in SolidWorks, AutoCAD, and engineering drawing/GD&T standards.","Practical understanding of manufacturing processes (machining, welding, sheet metal)."],"lo":1100,"hi":1800,"days":2,"hours":15},{"company":"Lawson & Reed","title":"Corporate Lawyer","description":"Lawson & Reed is a mid-market City of London law firm advising technology, finance, and industrial clients on M&A transactions, commercial contracts, regulatory compliance, and commercial disputes with partner-led teams. We're hiring a Corporate Lawyer to join the team (on-site, London, UK).\n\nAbout the role:\nLead mid-market UK M&A transactions, venture financings, shareholder agreements, and high-value commercial contracts in Lawson & Reed's City of London corporate team.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Run buy-side and sell-side private M&A transactions (£5M–£100M) from heads of terms through completion.\n- Draft and negotiate Share Purchase Agreements (SPAs), disclosure letters, shareholders' agreements, and commercial MSAs.\n- Lead legal due diligence streams and summarize key commercial risks clearly for founders and PE sponsors.\n- Supervise, train, and review drafting produced by junior associates, trainees, and paralegals.\n- Build trusted long-term advisory relationships with technology and industrial client boards.\n\nRequirements:\n- Qualified Solicitor (England & Wales) with 5+ years PQE in corporate / M&A practice.\n- Proven track record running mid-market transactions and complex commercial negotiations.\n- Sharp, commercial drafting clarity—able to distinguish real business risk from point-scoring.\n- Collaborative leadership with junior colleagues and client executives.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience advising SaaS, fintech, or cross-border European founders.\n- Familiarity with UK National Security and Investment (NSI) Act filings.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $5,200–$8,200 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- 25 days paid annual leave plus private Bupa medical and dental cover\n- Competitive City pension scheme and annual discretionary bonus\n- Hybrid London working (3 days in office) and season-ticket loan\n- Structured SQE/LPC training sponsorship and mentoring\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Legal","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"London, UK","skills":["Corporate Law","Contract Drafting","M&A","Negotiation","Legal Research"],"reqs":["Qualified Solicitor (England & Wales) with 5+ years PQE in corporate / M&A practice.","Proven track record running mid-market transactions and complex commercial negotiations.","Sharp, commercial drafting clarity—able to distinguish real business risk from point-scoring.","Collaborative leadership with junior colleagues and client executives."],