y interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Legal","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"London, UK","skills":["Legal Research","Document Review","Case Management","Writing","Confidentiality"],"reqs":["LLB Law degree (or GDL/PGDL) with strong academic record.","6+ months of paralegal or legal assistant experience (or clinical legal placement).","Exceptional proofreading eye, Microsoft Word formatting mastery, and deadline discipline.","High integrity and discretion with sensitive deal and dispute documents."],"lo":1100,"hi":1800,"days":16,"hours":1},{"company":"Lawson & Reed","title":"Legal Intern","description":"Lawson & Reed is a mid-market City of London law firm advising technology, finance, and industrial clients on M&A transactions, commercial contracts, regulatory compliance, and commercial disputes with partner-led teams. We're hiring a Legal Intern to join the team (on-site, London, UK).\n\nAbout the role:\nAn 8-week London vacation/legal internship rotating across Corporate and Commercial teams—giving aspiring solicitors real transaction research and drafting feedback.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Research discrete corporate, employment, or contract law questions and draft clear 1–2 page memos.\n- Assist paralegals and associates with document proofreading, contract schedules, and indexing.\n- Shadow client calls, negotiation sessions, and internal partner training seminars.\n- Complete two assessed written exercises with direct associate feedback.\n\nRequirements:\n- Undergraduate or postgraduate law student (or GDL/SQE candidate).\n- Clear, concise written English and analytical attention to detail.\n- Professional demeanor and enthusiasm to learn commercial legal practice in London.\n\nNice to have:\n- Participation in university mooting, negotiation competitions, or pro-bono legal clinics.\n- Demonstrated interest in technology or corporate law.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $450–$800 USD / month (Internship, On-site)\n- 25 days paid annual leave plus private Bupa medical and dental cover\n- Competitive City pension scheme and annual discretionary bonus\n- Hybrid London working (3 days in office) and season-ticket loan\n- Structured SQE/LPC training sponsorship and mentoring\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. Application & portfolio/CV review (2–3 business days)\n- 2. 30-minute conversation with your team mentor — focused on projects and curiosity, no trick questions\n- 3. Final placement confirmation and start-date onboarding","field":"Legal","seniority":"intern","type":"internship","mode":"onsite","location":"London, UK","skills":["Legal Research","Writing","Document Review"],"reqs":["Undergraduate or postgraduate law student (or GDL/SQE candidate).","Clear, concise written English and analytical attention to detail.","Professional demeanor and enthusiasm to learn commercial legal practice in London."],"lo":450,"hi":800,"days":2,"hours":6},{"company":"Peopleworks","title":"HR Generalist","description":"Peopleworks is an HR advisory, technical recruiting, and organizational learning partner helping high-growth tech and commercial companies across Egypt and MENA build healthy, high-performing teams. We're hiring a HR Generalist to join the team (hybrid, Cairo, Egypt).\n\nAbout the role:\nAct as dedicated embedded HR Partner for three growing tech and commercial client companies in Cairo—running onboarding, employee relations, and Egyptian labor-law compliance.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Manage end-to-end employee lifecycle operations—contracts, social insurance (Form 1/6), onboarding, and offboarding.\n- Advise client managers fairly on performance management, conflict resolution, and retention initiatives.\n- Maintain clean HRIS records, leave balances, and payroll inputs across client accounts.\n- Run structured quarterly check-ins and exit interviews to diagnose attrition drivers.\n- Ensure policies and handbooks remain compliant with Egyptian Labor Law.\n\nRequirements:\n- 3+ years of progressive HR Generalist or People Partner experience in Egypt.\n- Solid practical knowledge of Egyptian Labor Law, social insurance procedures, and HRIS tools.\n- Fluent Arabic and English with strong empathy, tact, and confidentiality.\n- Comfort juggling multiple client environments cleanly.\n\nNice to have:\n- HR Diploma (AUC, SHRM-CP, or CIPD Level 5).\n- Prior experience supporting SaaS or startup teams.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,300–$2,300 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- Private medical insurance and social insurance coverage from day one\n- 21 days paid annual leave plus flexible hybrid working days\n- Annual HR/CIPD/SHRM learning budget and performance commission\n- Collaborative Zamalek hub office with quiet interview pods\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"HR","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Cairo, Egypt","skills":["HR Operations","Employee Relations","Recruitment","Labor Law","HRIS"],"reqs":["3+ years of progressive HR Generalist or People Partner experience in Egypt.","Solid practical knowledge of Egyptian Labor Law, social insurance procedures, and HRIS tools.","Fluent Arabic and English with strong empathy, tact, and confidentiality.","Comfort juggling multiple client environments cleanly."],"lo":1300,"hi":2300,"days":9,"hours":11},{"company":"Peopleworks","title":"Talent Acquisition Specialist","description":"Peopleworks is an HR advisory, technical recruiting, and organizational learning partner helping high-growth tech and commercial companies across Egypt and MENA build healthy, high-performing teams. We're hiring a Talent Acquisition Specialist to join the team (remote).\n\nAbout the role:\nSource, screen, and close software, product, and commercial talent across MENA and Europe for Peopleworks' scaling client companies.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Partner with hiring managers to write honest, clear job briefs and calibrate interview scorecards.\n- Proactively source passive candidates via LinkedIn Recruiter, GitHub, and regional talent communities.\n- Conduct structured competency screens and deliver timely, respectful feedback to every applicant.\n- Manage ATS pipelines, coordinate interview panels, and guide offer negotiations cleanly.\n- Track time-to-hire, pass-through rates, and candidate experience scores.\n\nRequirements:\n- 2+ years of full-cycle technical or commercial recruiting in an agency or scaling startup.\n- Proven command of Boolean sourcing, LinkedIn Recruiter, and structured behavioral interviewing.\n- Warm, transparent candidate communication—never ghosting applicants.\n- Fluent English and Arabic.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience hiring software engineers, product designers, or data talent across MENA.\n- Familiarity with Greenhouse, Lever, or Ashby ATS.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,300–$2,300 USD / month (Full-time, Remote)\n- Private medical insurance and social insurance coverage from day one\n- 21 days paid annual leave plus flexible hybrid working days\n- Annual HR/CIPD/SHRM learning budget and performance commission\n- Collaborative Zamalek hub office with quiet interview pods\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"HR","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"remote","location":"Remote","skills":["Recruitment","Sourcing","Interviewing","LinkedIn Recruiter","Employer Branding"],"reqs":["2+ years of full-cycle technical or commercial recruiting in an agency or scaling startup.","Proven command of Boolean sourcing, LinkedIn Recruiter, 