ions, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"HR","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Cairo, Egypt","skills":["Training","Instructional Design","Communication","Event Planning"],"reqs":["1+ year in L&D coordination, HR administration, or educational program operations.","Strong organizational habits, visual slide polish, and warm facilitation support.","Fluent Arabic and English.","Genuine enthusiasm for adult learning and career development."],"lo":700,"hi":1200,"days":2,"hours":21},{"company":"Swiftline Logistics","title":"Business Development Manager","description":"Swiftline Logistics orchestrates ocean, road, and air freight forwarding plus bonded warehouse fulfillment out of Rotterdam for European retail and industrial manufacturers. Our operations and analytics teams manage customs clearance and real-time multimodal tracking. We're hiring a Business Development Manager to join the team (hybrid, Rotterdam, Netherlands).\n\nAbout the role:\nWin multi-year ocean, air, and bonded-warehousing contracts with European manufacturers and retailers importing through the Port of Rotterdam.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Identify and win mid-to-enterprise European importers/exporters needing reliable multimodal freight solutions.\n- Lead commercial RFP/RFQ responses alongside Swiftline's pricing, customs, and warehouse engineering teams.\n- Negotiate annual rate cards, SLA KPIs, fuel surcharges, and payment terms cleanly.\n- Grow share-of-wallet across newly won strategic accounts during their first 12 months.\n- Maintain accurate revenue forecasting and competitive market intelligence in Salesforce.\n\nRequirements:\n- 6+ years of B2B commercial sales experience in freight forwarding, 3PL warehousing, or supply chain.\n- Proven track record winning and expanding €500k+ annual logistics accounts.\n- Strong fluency in Incoterms 2020, ocean/air pricing structures, and European customs workflows.\n- Fluent English (Dutch or German is a major advantage).\n\nNice to have:\n- Established shipper relationships in retail, electronics, or industrial manufacturing.\n- Valid EU driving license for Benelux/DACH client visits.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $3,300–$5,000 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- 26 days paid vacation, 8% holiday pay, and Dutch pension scheme\n- Travel/commute allowance and free parking at our Maasvlakte & city hubs\n- Annual supply-chain & customs certification training budget\n- Clear growth paths into regional account and operations leadership\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Sales","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Rotterdam, Netherlands","skills":["Business Development","Negotiation","B2B Sales","Logistics","Client Management"],"reqs":["6+ years of B2B commercial sales experience in freight forwarding, 3PL warehousing, or supply chain.","Proven track record winning and expanding €500k+ annual logistics accounts.","Strong fluency in Incoterms 2020, ocean/air pricing structures, and European customs workflows.","Fluent English (Dutch or German is a major advantage)."],"lo":3300,"hi":5000,"days":9,"hours":2},{"company":"Bluewave Hotels","title":"Sales Executive","description":"Bluewave Hotels operates 14 beachfront resorts and urban lifestyle hotels across the UAE, Oman, and Bahrain. Known for warm service and vibrant dining concepts, we employ over 2,400 hospitality professionals across rooms, culinary, revenue, and guest experience. We're hiring a Sales Executive to join the team (on-site, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nDrive corporate room-night accounts, small MICE conferences, and wedding/group bookings for two flagship Bluewave beachfront properties in Dubai.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Prospect local corporates, travel agencies, and event planners for room blocks and meeting-room packages.\n- Conduct warm, polished hotel site inspections showcasing suites, ballrooms, and beachfront venues.\n- Prepare tailored proposals and coordinate event BEO handoffs smoothly with banquet and front-office teams.\n- Follow up promptly on inbound RFPs and log all account activity in Opera Sales & Catering.\n- Represent Bluewave professionally at regional trade networking mixers.\n\nRequirements:\n- 1–2 years in hotel sales, events coordination, or B2B hospitality.\n- Warm, polished presentation skills and prompt client follow-through.\n- Fluent spoken and written English; Arabic or another international language is a plus.\n- Comfortable working on-site across our Dubai properties.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience with Opera PMS / Sales & Catering or Delphi.\n- Existing familiarity with Dubai corporate/MICE agencies.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,100–$1,800 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Medical insurance, duty meals, and staff accommodation or housing allowance\n- 30 days paid annual leave plus annual return flight ticket\n- Preferential friends-and-family room & dining rates across all 14 properties\n- Service-charge share and cross-property career mobility\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Sales","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Sales","Customer Service","CRM","Hospitality","Communication"],"reqs":["1–2 years in hotel sales, events coordination, or B2B hospitality.","Warm, polished presentation skills and prompt client follow-through.","Fluent spoken and written English; Arabic or another international language is a plus.","Comfortable working on-site across our Dubai properties."],"lo":1100,"hi":1800,"days":16,"hours":7},{"company":"Bluewave Hotels","title":"Front Office Manager","description":"Bluewave Hotels operates 14 beachfront resorts and urban lifestyle hotels across the UAE, Oman, and Bahrain. Known for warm service and vibrant dining concepts, we employ over 2,400 hospitality professionals across rooms, culinary, revenue, and guest experience. We're hiring a Front Office Manager to join the team (on-site, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nLead a 24-person Reception, Bell/Concierge, and Night Audit brigade at a 280-key Bluewave resort in Dubai—ensuring effortless arrivals and 4.8+ guest review scores.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Oversee daily front-desk, concierge, bell-service, and night-audit operations across rotating shifts.\n- Coach front-office associates on genuine hospitality, VIP personalization, and tasteful room-upsell targets.\n- Resolve complex guest service recoveries calmly on the spot to turn issues into loyalty.\n- Audit daily Opera PMS room inventory, cash/card reconciliations, and VIP arrival amenities.\n- Monitor Booking.com, TripAdvisor, and post-stay surveys weekly to close service gaps.\n\nRequirements:\n- 3+ years in luxury or upper-upscale hotel Front Office operations, including 1+ year as Assistant FOM or Duty Manager.\n- Strong hands-on mastery of Opera PMS and hotel night-audit controls.\n- Fluent English (Arabic, Russian, or French highly valued).\n- Inspiring floor leadership during high-occupancy weekends and peak seasons.\n\nNice to have:\n- Bachelor's degree in Hospitality Management.\n- GCC 5-star beachfront resort experience.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Medical insurance, duty meals, and staff accommodation or housing allowance\n- 30 days paid annual leave plus annual return flight ticket\n- Preferential friends-and-family room & dining rates across all 14 properties\n- Service-charge share and cross-property career mobility\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Hospitality","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Hotel Operations","Customer Service","Team Leadership","Opera PMS","Upselling"],"reqs":["3+ years in luxury or upper-upscale hotel Front Office operations, including 1+ year as Assistant FOM or Duty Manager.","Strong hands-on mastery of Opera PMS and hotel night-audit controls.","Fluent English (Arabic, Russian, or French highly valued).","Inspiring floor leadership during high-occupancy weekends and peak seasons."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":2,"hours":12},{"company":"Bluewave Hotels","title":"Sous Chef","description":"Bluewave Hotels operates 14 beachfront resorts and urban lifestyle hotels across the UAE, Oman, and Bahrain. Known for warm service and vibrant dining concepts, we employ over 2,400 hospitality professionals across rooms, culinary, revenue, and guest experience. We're hiring a Sous Chef to join the team (on-site, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nPartner with our Executive Chef to run a vibrant 35-cook Mediterranean & Levantine kitchen serving all-day dining, poolside grill, and private events in Dubai.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Lead hot-line pass execution during peak lunch and dinner services to keep ticket times and plating spotless.\n- Train, schedule, and mentor Demi Chefs and Commis cooks across prep, hygiene, and knife skills.\n- Manage daily market ordering, par levels, portion consistency, and food-cost waste logs.\n- Enforce strict Dubai Municipality HACCP food-safety, labeling, and cold-storage logs.\n- Collaborate with the Executive Chef on seasonal specials and tasting menus.\n\nRequirements:\n- 4+ years of