2,400 hospitality professionals across rooms, culinary, revenue, and guest experience. We're hiring a Guest Relations Agent to join the team (on-site, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nCraft memorable moments for international resort guests in Dubai—handling pre-arrival preferences, celebratory room touches, concierge bookings, and warm check-ins.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Reach out to VIP and special-occasion guests pre-arrival to personalize transfers, pillows, and dining plans.\n- Greet guests warmly in the lobby, coordinate seamless express check-ins, and escort VIPs to rooms.\n- Arrange desert safaris, restaurant tables, spa slots, and yacht charters accurately.\n- Check in mid-stay with guests to catch small issues early and elevate their holiday.\n- Log guest preferences faithfully in Opera CRM for future stays across Bluewave properties.\n\nRequirements:\n- 1+ year in luxury hospitality, airline cabin crew, or high-touch concierge service.\n- Warm, genuine presence and calm problem solving when requests change last minute.\n- Fluent English plus strong proficiency in at least one additional language (Arabic, French, German, or Russian).\n- Flexible availability across rotating resort shifts.\n\nNice to have:\n- Familiarity with Opera PMS and Alice/HotSOS guest-request platforms.\n- Deep insider knowledge of Dubai dining and cultural attractions.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,100–$1,800 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Medical insurance, duty meals, and staff accommodation or housing allowance\n- 30 days paid annual leave plus annual return flight ticket\n- Preferential friends-and-family room & dining rates across all 14 properties\n- Service-charge share and cross-property career mobility\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Hospitality","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Customer Service","Communication","Problem Solving","Languages"],"reqs":["1+ year in luxury hospitality, airline cabin crew, or high-touch concierge service.","Warm, genuine presence and calm problem solving when requests change last minute.","Fluent English plus strong proficiency in at least one additional language (Arabic, French, German, or Russian).","Flexible availability across rotating resort shifts."],"lo":1100,"hi":1800,"days":16,"hours":22},{"company":"Bluewave Hotels","title":"Revenue Manager","description":"Bluewave Hotels operates 14 beachfront resorts and urban lifestyle hotels across the UAE, Oman, and Bahrain. Known for warm service and vibrant dining concepts, we employ over 2,400 hospitality professionals across rooms, culinary, revenue, and guest experience. We're hiring a Revenue Manager to join the team (hybrid, Dubai, UAE).\n\nAbout the role:\nOptimize RevPAR, ADR, and channel mix across a cluster of Bluewave properties from our Dubai corporate office—balancing OTA, direct web, corporate, and tour-operator demand.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Manage daily dynamic pricing, length-of-stay restrictions, and room-type differentials across assigned properties.\n- Build 90-day and annual rolling demand, ADR, and RevPAR forecasts by market segment.\n- Evaluate group/MICE displacement analyses alongside Sales before approving large discounted blocks.\n- Audit OTA parity, metasearch performance, and direct-booking conversion alongside Digital Marketing.\n- Chair weekly revenue strategy meetings with Hotel General Managers and Commercial Directors.\n\nRequirements:\n- 5+ years in hotel revenue management, preferably managing multi-property clusters or large resorts.\n- Expert analytical command of Excel, RMS platforms (IDeaS/Duetto), STR benchmarking, and Opera PMS.\n- Strong commercial instincts around seasonality, events, and distribution costs.\n- Clear executive presentation skills.\n\nNice to have:\n- GCC resort & city-hotel dual-market experience.\n- SQL or Power BI dashboarding skills.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $3,300–$5,000 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- Medical insurance, duty meals, and staff accommodation or housing allowance\n- 30 days paid annual leave plus annual return flight ticket\n- Preferential friends-and-family room & dining rates across all 14 properties\n- Service-charge share and cross-property career mobility\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Hospitality","seniority":"senior","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Dubai, UAE","skills":["Revenue Management","Pricing","Excel","Forecasting","Hospitality"],"reqs":["5+ years in hotel revenue management, preferably managing multi-property clusters or large resorts.","Expert analytical command of Excel, RMS platforms (IDeaS/Duetto), STR benchmarking, and Opera PMS.","Strong commercial instincts around seasonality, events, and distribution costs.","Clear executive presentation skills."],"lo":3300,"hi":5000,"days":2,"hours":3},{"company":"Swiftline Logistics","title":"Supply Chain Analyst","description":"Swiftline Logistics orchestrates ocean, road, and air freight forwarding plus bonded warehouse fulfillment out of Rotterdam for European retail and industrial manufacturers. Our operations and analytics teams manage customs clearance and real-time multimodal tracking. We're hiring a Supply Chain Analyst to join the team (hybrid, Rotterdam, Netherlands).\n\nAbout the role:\nAnalyze container transit times, port dwell bottlenecks, and bonded warehouse stock turns out of Rotterdam to cut freight spend and improve on-time-in-full (OTIF) delivery.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Query shipment, carrier, and warehouse KPIs across SAP/WMS and SQL to diagnose delays and detention/demurrage costs.\n- Build weekly carrier scorecards and lane-cost benchmarks across sea, road, and air corridors.\n- Forecast seasonal warehouse labor and pallet-capacity requirements for key retail accounts.\n- Model route-consolidation and inventory-rebalancing scenarios to lower client freight spend.\n- Present clear operational savings decks directly to account managers and enterprise shippers.\n\nRequirements:\n- 2+ years in supply chain, freight, or inventory analytics.\n- Strong SQL, advanced Excel, and ERP/WMS (SAP MM/SD/EWM) data fluency.\n- Solid understanding of multimodal freight KPIs (OTIF, dwell time, load factor, landed cost).\n- Clear analytical storytelling in English.\n\nNice to have:\n- Power BI or Python automation experience.\n- Dutch language skills.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $2,000–$3,300 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- 26 days paid vacation, 8% holiday pay, and Dutch pension scheme\n- Travel/commute allowance and free parking at our Maasvlakte & city hubs\n- Annual supply-chain & customs certification training budget\n- Clear growth paths into regional account and operations leadership\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Logistics","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Rotterdam, Netherlands","skills":["Supply Chain","Excel","SQL","Forecasting","SAP"],"reqs":["2+ years in supply chain, freight, or inventory analytics.","Strong SQL, advanced Excel, and ERP/WMS (SAP MM/SD/EWM) data fluency.","Solid understanding of multimodal freight KPIs (OTIF, dwell time, load factor, landed cost).","Clear analytical storytelling in English."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":9,"hours":8},{"company":"Swiftline Logistics","title":"Procurement Officer","descrip