nager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Logistics","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Rotterdam, Netherlands","skills":["Procurement","Negotiation","Vendor Management","SAP","Contract Management"],"reqs":["3+ years in logistics procurement, carrier buying, or indirect/direct purchasing.","Strong commercial negotiation skills and hands-on SAP procurement experience.","High attention to contract terms, total cost of ownership (TCO), and compliance.","Fluent English (Dutch or German is an asset)."],"lo":2000,"hi":3300,"days":16,"hours":13},{"company":"Swiftline Logistics","title":"Warehouse Supervisor","description":"Swiftline Logistics orchestrates ocean, road, and air freight forwarding plus bonded warehouse fulfillment out of Rotterdam for European retail and industrial manufacturers. Our operations and analytics teams manage customs clearance and real-time multimodal tracking. We're hiring a Warehouse Supervisor to join the team (on-site, Rotterdam, Netherlands).\n\nAbout the role:\nLead a 15-person inbound, pick-pack, and outbound dock shift at our bonded Rotterdam distribution center—keeping inventory >99.7% accurate and docks accident-free.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Allocate daily shift staff across receiving, put-away, RF picking, cross-docking, and container loading.\n- Verify WMS cycle counts, investigate stock discrepancies immediately, and keep FIFO/FEFO order.\n- Enforce strict forklift pedestrian-lane safety, PPE compliance, and dock-lock procedures.\n- Run crisp 10-minute shift handoff briefings tracking pallets/hour and SLA cut-offs.\n- Onboard new warehouse associates and cross-train staff on reach-truck and scanner workflows.\n\nRequirements:\n- 2+ years in warehouse operations, including 1+ year as Team Lead or Shift Supervisor.\n- Hands-on proficiency with RF barcode scanners and Warehouse Management Systems (WMS).\n- Strong safety-first floor presence and fair, clear people leadership.\n- Comfortable working early or late warehouse shift patterns in Rotterdam.\n\nNice to have:\n- Valid Dutch forklift / reach-truck certificate and BHV first-aid training.\n- Conversational Dutch alongside English.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,100–$1,800 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- 26 days paid vacation, 8% holiday pay, and Dutch pension scheme\n- Travel/commute allowance and free parking at our Maasvlakte & city hubs\n- Annual supply-chain & customs certification training budget\n- Clear growth paths into regional account and operations leadership\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Logistics","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Rotterdam, Netherlands","skills":["Warehouse Operations","Inventory Management","Team Leadership","Safety"],"reqs":["2+ years in warehouse operations, including 1+ year as Team Lead or Shift Supervisor.","Hands-on proficiency with RF barcode scanners and Warehouse Management Systems (WMS).","Strong safety-first floor presence and fair, clear people leadership.","Comfortable working early or late warehouse shift patterns in Rotterdam."],"lo":1100,"hi":1800,"days":2,"hours":18},{"company":"Swiftline Logistics","title":"Logistics Coordinator","description":"Swiftline Logistics orchestrates ocean, road, and air freight forwarding plus bonded warehouse fulfillment out of Rotterdam for European retail and industrial manufacturers. Our operations and analytics teams manage customs clearance and real-time multimodal tracking. We're hiring a Logistics Coordinator to join the team (on-site, Rotterdam, Netherlands).\n\nAbout the role:\nCoordinate end-to-end sea and road import shipments passing through Rotterdam—booking drayage, checking customs documents, and keeping clients updated without surprises.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Book container drayage, LTL/FTL road pickups, and ocean/air slot allocations with carriers.\n- Verify Bills of Lading, commercial invoices, packing lists, and EUR.1 / T1 customs paperwork prior to arrival.\n- Monitor vessel ETAs and customs releases proactively, escalating holds or demurrage risks early.\n- Send clear, accurate shipment status updates and PODs to shipper customers.\n- Update TMS job files cleanly for accurate billing.\n\nRequirements:\n- 1+ year in freight forwarding, import/export coordination, or transport planning.\n- Familiarity with Incoterms, Bills of Lading, and EU customs documentation.\n- Strong Excel and multitasking accuracy under port cut-off deadlines.\n- Fluent English (Dutch helpful).\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience with CargoWise or European customs portals.\n- Degree or diploma in International Trade / Logistics.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,100–$1,800 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- 26 days paid vacation, 8% holiday pay, and Dutch pension scheme\n- Travel/commute allowance and free parking at our Maasvlakte & city hubs\n- Annual supply-chain & customs certification training budget\n- Clear growth paths into regional account and operations leadership\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Logistics","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Rotterdam, Netherlands","skills":["Logistics","Scheduling","Customs","Excel","Communication"],"reqs":["1+ year in freight forwarding, import/export coordination, or transport planning.","Familiarity with Incoterms, Bills of Lading, and EU customs documentation.","Strong Excel and multitasking accuracy under port cut-off deadlines.","Fluent English (Dutch helpful)."],"lo":1100,"hi":1800,"days":9,"hours":23},{"company":"Daily Ledger Media","title":"Journalist","description":"Daily Ledger Media publishes an independent bilingual Arabic–English business and current-affairs news site alongside a flagship weekly investigative video show. From our Beirut newsroom, 65 journalists, video producers, translators, and web engineers serve over 1.8 million monthly readers. We're hiring a Journalist to join the team (hybrid, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nReport deeply on Lebanese and regional economy, banking, energy, and tech accountability stories for Daily Ledger's bilingual digital edition in Beirut.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Pitch, report, and write 3–4 original news analyses and enterprise features per week.\n- Cultivate reliable primary sources across ministries, businesses, economists, and civil society.\n- Verify every figure, public tender, and quote rigorously in partnership with our fact-checking desk.\n- Collaborate with data journalists and video producers to adapt investigations across text and video.\n- File clean copy reliably under breaking-news and daily edition deadlines.\n\nRequirements:\n- 3+ years of published journalism experience covering business, economics, policy, or investigative beats.\n- Portfolio of 4+ strong published clips demonstrating original sourcing and clear storytelling.\n- Strong command of both Arabic and English reporting/writing.\n- Uncompromising editorial ethics, source protection, and accuracy under deadline pressure.\n\nNice to have:\n- Data-journalism comfort (reading budgets, corporate registries, spreadsheets).\n- Experience appearing on podcasts or short video explainers.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,300–$2,300 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- Private medical insurance and 20 days paid annual leave\n- Press credentials, editorial safety training, and travel expense coverage\n- Modern Mac/PC workstation and access to our Beirut studio & archive\n- Collaborative newsroom culture with real editorial independence\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Media","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["Journalism","Writing","Research","Interviewing","Fact-checking"],"reqs":["3+ years of published journalism experience covering business, economics, policy, or investigative beats.","Portfolio of 4+ strong published clips demonstrating original sourcing and clear storytelling.","Strong command of both Arabic and English reporting/writing.","Uncompromising editorial ethics, source protection, and accuracy under deadline pressure."],"lo":1300,"hi":2300,"days":16,"hours":4},{"company":"Daily Ledger Media","title":"Video Producer","description":"Daily Ledger Media publishes an independent bilingual Arabic–English business and current-affairs news site alongside a flagship weekly investigative video show. From our Beirut newsroom, 65 journalists, video producers, translators, and web engineers serve over 1.8 million monthly readers. We're hiring a Video Producer to join the team (on-site, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nProduce, shoot, and edit Daily Ledger's flagship weekly 15-minute investigative video show and sharp vertical social explainers from our Beirut studio and on location.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Plan weekly episode scripts, interview setups, archival B-roll, and visual pacing with senior editors.\n- Operate cinema cameras, studio lighting, and wireless lavalier/boom audio cleanly on field shoots.\n- Edit tight, engaging episodes in Adobe Premiere Pro with clean color grading, sound mixing, and bilingual lower-thirds.\n- Cut vertical 9:16 social trailers and explainer clips tailored for YouTube Shorts and Instagram Reels.\n- Manage media ingest, project backups, and weekly broadcast upload deadlines.\n\nRequirements:\n- 2+ years producing and editing documentary, news, or digital explainer video.\n- A strong showreel demonstrating narrative pacing, clean audio, and visual polish.\n- Expert proficiency in Adobe Premiere Pro (and basic After Effects / Audition).\n- Fluent Arabic and English with calm composure on fast-moving field shoots.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience operating Sony FX3/FX6 cameras and DaVinci Resolve.\n- Motion-graphics skills for data-driven map/chart explainers.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,300–$2,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Private medical insurance and 20 days paid annual leave\n- Press credentials, editorial safety training, and travel expense coverage\n- Modern Mac/PC workstation and access to our Beirut studio & archive\n- Collaborative newsroom culture with real editorial independence\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Media","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["Video Production","Premiere Pro","Storytelling","Camera Operation","Editing"],"reqs":["2+ years producing and editing documentary, news, or digital explainer video.","A strong showreel demonstrating narrative pacing, clean audio, and visual polish.","Expert proficiency in Adobe Premiere Pro (and basic After Effects / Audition).","Fluent Arabic and English with calm composure on fast-moving field shoots."],"lo":1300,"hi":2300,"days":2,"hours":9},{"company":"Daily Ledger Media","title":"Translator (Arabic–English)","description":"Daily Ledger Media publishes an independent bilingual Arabic–English business and current-affairs news site alongside a flagship weekly investigative video show. From our Beirut newsroom, 65 journalists, video producers, translators, and web engineers serve over 1.8 million monthly readers. We're hiring a Translator (Arabic–English) to join the team (remote).\n\nAbout the role:\nTranslate Daily Ledger's investigative features, economic analyses, and video subtitles seamlessly between Arabic and English—preserving nuance, tone, and journalistic precision.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Translate 1,500–2,500 words per day of news features, opinion columns, and investigative reports both ways (AR↔EN).\n- Localize financial, legal, and regional policy terminology accurately without stiff literal phrasing.\n- Translate and time-sync SRT subtitle files for weekly video episodes and social clips.\n- Proofread translated drafts against house style guides and verify proper names/titles.\n- Meet fast same-day publishing turnarounds for priority news stories.\n\nRequirements:\n- 3+ years of professional Arabic–English editorial, journalism, or policy translation experience.\n- Native-level mastery of both Modern Standard Arabic and idiomatic journalistic English.\n- Sharp eye for register, nuance, and factual accuracy.\n- Reliable remote availability to handle same-day newsroom turnarounds.\n\nNice to have:\n- Degree in Translation, Linguistics, or Journalism.\n- Experience translating financial/economic reports or subtitle files (SRT).\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,300–$2,300 USD / month (Contract, Remote)\n- Private medical insurance and 20 days paid annual leave\n- Press credentials, editorial safety training, and travel expense coverage\n- Modern Mac/PC workstation and access to our Beirut studio & archive\n- Collaborative newsroom culture with real editorial independence\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Media","seniority":"mid","type":"contract","mode":"remote","location":"Remote","skills":["Translation","Arabic","English","Editing","Localization"],"reqs":["3+ years of professional Arabic–English editorial, journalism, or policy translation experience.","Native-level mastery of both Modern Standard Arabic and idiomatic journalistic English.","Sharp eye for register, nuance, and factual accuracy.","Reliable remote availability to handle same-day newsroom turnarounds."],"lo":1300,"hi":2300,"days":9,"hours":14},{"company":"Daily Ledger Media","title":"Social Media Editor","description":"Daily Ledger Media publishes an independent bilingual Arabic–English business and current-affairs news site alongside a flagship weekly investigative video show. From our Beirut newsroom, 65 journalists, video producers, translators, and web engineers serve over 1.8 million monthly readers. We're hiring a Social Media Editor to join the team (hybrid, Beirut, Lebanon).\n\nAbout the role:\nPackage Daily Ledger's journalism for social readers across Instagram, X, YouTube, and WhatsApp Channels—writing sharp bilingual hooks and growing loyal audience reach.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Turn daily articles and weekly videos into punchy carousel posts, threads, and short-form social teasers.\n- Write accurate, high-curiosity headlines and captions in Arabic and English without clickbait distortion.\n- Monitor breaking-news conversations and coordinate live updates during major regional developments.\n- Track audience retention, click-through rates, and share velocity to refine publishing formats.\n- Moderate comments constructively and surface reader questions back to the reporting desk.\n\nRequirements:\n- 1+ year managing social channels for a newsroom, publication, or media brand.\n- Sharp editorial judgment and fluent writing in both Arabic and English.\n- Hands-on comfort with Canva/Figma templates and native platform analytics.\n- Calm, accurate speed when publishing breaking stories.\n\nNice to have:\n- Basic CapCut or Premiere clip-cutting experience.\n- Familiarity with SEO/Google Discover headline testing.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $700–$1,200 USD / month (Full-time, Hybrid)\n- Private medical insurance and 20 days paid annual leave\n- Press credentials, editorial safety training, and travel expense coverage\n- Modern Mac/PC workstation and access to our Beirut studio & archive\n- Collaborative newsroom culture with real editorial independence\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Media","seniority":"junior","type":"full_time","mode":"hybrid","location":"Beirut, Lebanon","skills":["Social Media","Copywriting","Content Strategy","Analytics"],"reqs":["1+ year managing social channels for a newsroom, publication, or media brand.","Sharp editorial judgment and fluent writing in both Arabic and English.","Hands-on comfort with Canva/Figma templates and native platform analytics.","Calm, accurate speed when publishing breaking stories."],"lo":700,"hi":1200,"days":16,"hours":19},{"company":"Brightpath Academy","title":"Computer Science Teacher","description":"Brightpath Academy is a bilingual K–12 international school serving 950 students in Amman alongside a growing blended online learning division. Our faculty emphasizes inquiry-led STEM, strong literacy foundations, and individualized student mentoring. We're hiring a Computer Science Teacher to join the team (on-site, Amman, Jordan).\n\nAbout the role:\nTeach Python programming, algorithms, web fundamentals, and digital literacy to Grades 8–12 in Amman while mentoring our after-school robotics and coding club.\n\nWhat you'll do:\n- Deliver project-based Computer Science lessons covering Python, data structures, HTML/CSS, and databases.\n- Prepare senior students thoroughly for IGCSE / IB / AP Computer Science practical and written exams.\n- Design engaging coding labs, debugging challenges, and rubric-graded capstone apps.\n- Lead the weekly student coding & hackathon club and coach teams for regional competitions.\n- Track individual mastery and collaborate with math and science faculty on interdisciplinary STEM projects.\n\nRequirements:\n- Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or IT Education.\n- 2+ years teaching secondary Computer Science (or software engineering experience paired with strong mentoring/teaching).\n- Strong fluency in Python and foundational web/database concepts.\n- Fluent English instruction skills and patient, encouraging classroom presence.\n\nNice to have:\n- Experience teaching IGCSE, IB DP, or AP Computer Science A.\n- Interest in robotics (Arduino/micro:bit) or responsible AI literacy.\n\nCompensation & benefits:\n- Monthly salary: $1,300–$2,300 USD / month (Full-time, On-site)\n- Comprehensive medical insurance and tuition discount for faculty children\n- Full school-calendar winter and summer breaks plus paid professional development\n- Relocation and housing guidance for international educators\n- Dedicated classroom technology budget and collaborative prep periods\n\nHiring process:\n- 1. 25-minute intro call on role expectations, schedule, and monthly salary range\n- 2. Role-specific practical case or competency interview with the hiring manager\n- 3. Final team & leadership alignment conversation","field":"Education","seniority":"mid","type":"full_time","mode":"onsite","location":"Amman, Jordan","skills":["Teaching","Computer Science","Python","Lesson Planning","Classroom Management"],"reqs":["Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or IT Education.","2+ years teaching secondary Computer Science (or software engineering experience paired with strong mentoring/teaching).","Strong fluency in Python and foundational web/database concepts.","Fluent English instruction skills and patient, encouraging classroom presence."],"lo":1300,"hi":2300,"days":2,"hours":0}]$seed$::jsonb) as x(
    company text, title text, description text, field text, seniority text, type text, mode text,
    location text, skills text[], reqs text[], lo int, hi int, days int, hours int)
),
upd_j as (
  update public.jobs e
  set
    description = j.description,
    requirements = j.reqs,
    skills = j.skills,
    field = j.field,
    seniority = j.seniority::public.seniority,
    employment_type = j.type::public.employment_type,
    work_mode = j.mode::public.work_mode,
    location = j.location,
    salary_min = j.lo,
    salary_max = j.hi,
    salary_currency = 'USD'
  from src_j j
  join all_c c on c.name = j.company
  where e.is_demo and e.company_id = c.id and e.title = j.title
  returning e.id
)
insert into public.jobs (company_id, title, description, requirements, skills, field, seniority, employment_type, work_mode, location, salary_min, salary_max, salary_currency, status, is_demo, published_at)
select
  c.id,
  j.title,
  j.description,
  j.reqs,
  j.skills,
  j.field,
  j.seniority::public.seniority,
  j.type::public.employment_type,
  j.mode::public.work_mode,
  j.location,
  j.lo,
  j.hi,
  'USD',
  'open'::public.job_status,
  true,
  now() - make_interval(days => j.days, hours => j.hours)
from src_j j
join all_c c on c.name = j.company
where not exists (
  select 1 from public.jobs e join public.companies ec on ec.id = e.company_id
  where e.is_demo and ec.name = j.company and e.title = j.title
);
